role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Research Counter. Recap: shared path exists with README but no raw logs yet. I’ll read the README, persist a safe combiner script to shared storage, then run it to produce a small JSONL sample (gracefully handling no logs).\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/README_collect.md}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/logs_to_jsonl_v0_3.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  # logs_to_jsonl_v0_3.py\n  import os, json, gzip\n\n  DEFAULT_ROOT = 'storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs'\n  DEFAULT_OUT = os.path.join(DEFAULT_ROOT, 'combined_sample.jsonl')\n\n  def _open(path):\n    if path.endswith('.gz'):\n      return gzip.open(path, 'rt', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore')\n    return open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore')\n\n  def _iter_files(root):\n    for dirpath, _, filenames in os.walk(root):\n      for fn in filenames:\n\
    \        p = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\n        low = fn.lower()\n        if low.endswith(('.jsonl', '.json', '.log', '.txt', '.jsonl.gz', '.json.gz', '.log.gz', '.txt.gz')):\n          yield p\n\n  def _iter_records_from_file(path):\n    rel = path\n    try:\n      if path.endswith(('.jsonl', '.log', '.txt', '.jsonl.gz', '.log.gz', '.txt.gz')):\n        with _open(path) as f:\n          for i, line in enumerate(f, 1):\n            line = line.strip()\n            if not line:\n              continue\n            try:\n              rec = json.loads(line)\n            except Exception:\n              rec = {'raw': line}\n            if isinstance(rec, dict):\n              rec.setdefault('_source_file', rel)\n              rec.setdefault('_line_no', i)\n              yield rec\n            else:\n              yield {'value': rec, '_source_file': rel, '_line_no': i}\n      else:  # .json or .json.gz\n        with _open(path) as f:\n          obj = json.load(f)\n        if isinstance(obj,\
    \ list):\n          for idx, item in enumerate(obj):\n            if isinstance(item, dict):\n              item.setdefault('_source_file', rel)\n              item.setdefault('_item_index', idx)\n              yield item\n            else:\n              yield {'value': item, '_source_file': rel, '_item_index': idx}\n        elif isinstance(obj, dict):\n          obj = dict(obj)\n          obj.setdefault('_source_file', rel)\n          yield obj\n        else:\n          yield {'value': obj, '_source_file': rel}\n    except Exception as e:\n      yield {'_error': str(e), '_source_file': rel}\n\n  def run(root=DEFAULT_ROOT, out_path=DEFAULT_OUT, max_records=200):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n    files = list(_iter_files(root))\n    written = 0\n    errors = 0\n    with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as out_f:\n      for path in files:\n        for rec in _iter_records_from_file(path):\n          if '_error' in rec:\n            errors += 1\n    \
    \        continue\n          out_f.write(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n          written += 1\n          if written >= max_records:\n            break\n        if written >= max_records:\n          break\n    return {\n      'root': root,\n      'out_path': out_path,\n      'files_scanned': len(files),\n      'records_written': written,\n      'errors': errors\n    }\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n    import argparse\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument('--root', default=DEFAULT_ROOT)\n    p.add_argument('--out', default=DEFAULT_OUT)\n    p.add_argument('--max', dest='max_records', type=int, default=200)\n    args = p.parse_args()\n    summary = run(root=args.root, out_path=args.out, max_records=args.max_records)\n    print(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Run shared logs combiner v0_3 (sample JSONL)\"\ntags: \"data engineering, logs, jsonl, aggregator, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Runs a safe\
    \ combiner over shared progressor/raw_eval_logs and emits a JSONL sample (≤200 records). Handles json/jsonl/txt/log and .gz, annotates source, and prints a summary.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs')\n  from logs_to_jsonl_v0_3 import run\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      summary = run(max_records=200)\n      print(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n```"
