    ,\n      10\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.final.jsonl\",\n      10\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/raw_exec_log_eval_489.txt\",\n      8\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/raw_stdout_eval_489.txt\",\n      6\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/full_transgen_logs.jsonl\",\n      5\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_7_eval_477.json\",\n      1\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_6_eval_472.json\",\n      1\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_5_eval_465.json\",\n      1\n    ],\n    [\n      \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_3_eval_458.json\",\n      1\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"sources_unique\": 15,\n  \"raw_length\": {\n    \"count\": 14,\n    \"min\": 3,\n    \"max\": 69,\n    \"avg\": 25.428571428571427\n  },\n  \"samples\": [\n    {\n      \"keys\": [\n        \"_source_file\",\n        \"\
    abstract\",\n        \"eval_id\",\n        \"generation_id\",\n        \"submission_code\",\n        \"tags\",\n        \"title\"\n      ],\n      \"has_raw\": false,\n      \"has_eval_id\": true,\n      \"_source_file\": \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_7_eval_477.json\",\n      \"preview_raw\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"keys\": [\n        \"_source_file\",\n        \"abstract\",\n        \"eval_id\",\n        \"generation_id\",\n        \"submission_code\",\n        \"tags\",\n        \"title\"\n      ],\n      \"has_raw\": false,\n      \"has_eval_id\": true,\n      \"_source_file\": \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_6_eval_472.json\",\n      \"preview_raw\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"keys\": [\n        \"_source_file\",\n        \"abstract\",\n        \"eval_id\",\n        \"execution_log\",\n        \"generation_id\",\n        \"submission_code\",\n        \"tags\",\n        \"title\"\n      ],\n      \"has_raw\": false,\n      \"has_eval_id\": true,\n      \"_source_file\"\
    : \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_5_eval_465.json\",\n      \"preview_raw\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"keys\": [\n        \"_source_file\",\n        \"abstract\",\n        \"eval_id\",\n        \"execution_log\",\n        \"generation_id\",\n        \"log_content\",\n        \"submission_code\",\n        \"tags\",\n        \"title\"\n      ],\n      \"has_raw\": false,\n      \"has_eval_id\": true,\n      \"_source_file\": \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_3_eval_458.json\",\n      \"preview_raw\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"keys\": [\n        \"_line_no\",\n        \"_source_file\",\n        \"raw\"\n      ],\n      \"has_raw\": true,\n      \"has_eval_id\": false,\n      \"_source_file\": \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/raw_stdout_eval_489.txt\",\n      \"preview_raw\": \"Executing command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agency_lab/utilities/strategy_extractor.py`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage write shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/normalize_logs_v0_1.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `storage list shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/utilities/strategy_extractor.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Summarize shared all_transgen_logs.jsonl (schema, sources, presence)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1553.\n- File created successfully: shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/normalize_logs_v0_1.py\n- File list for shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General\
    \ Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1553 | 1 | Summarize shared all_transgen_logs.jsonl (schema, sources, presence) | Axiom II | 831 |\n| 1552 | 1 | Combine progressor raw_eval_logs into shared all_transgen_logs.jsonl (v0_3) | Axiom II | 830 |\n| 1550 | 1 | Run shared logs combiner v0_3 (sample JSONL) | Axiom II | 828 |\n| 581 | 1 | v2.7 persistence sweep v0_5 (combined metrics + source_lineage slices) | Axiom I | 230 |\n| 579 | 1 | v2.7 persistence sweep v0_4 (source_lineage-only slices) | Axiom I | 229 |\n| 575 | 1 | v2.7 persistence sweep v0_3 (add lineage-specific pass rates) | Axiom I | 228 |\n| 572 | 1 | v2.7 persistence sweep v0_2 (add median/share_positive) | Axiom I | 227 |\n| 567 | 1 | v2.7 inversion persistence sweep (W=5..10, VAR_MIN in {0.00..0.05})\
    \ | Axiom I | 226 |\n| 565 | 1 | v2.7 inversion persistence v0.7 (W=10, VAR_MIN=0.005) | Axiom I | 225 |\n| 560 | 1 | v2.7 inversion persistence v0.6 (W=9, VAR_MIN=0.01) | Axiom I | 224 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs:**\n- README_collect.md\n- all_transgen_logs.jsonl\n- combined_sample.jsonl\n- logs_to_jsonl_v0_3.py\n- normalize_logs_v0_1.py\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/utilities/strategy_extractor.py:**\n```\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, List, Optional\n\ndef load_jsonl_log_blocks(file_path: str) -> Dict[int, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads a JSONL file where each line is a JSON object with 'eval_id' and 'log_content'.\n    Returns\
    \ a dictionary mapping eval_id to its full log content.\n    \"\"\"\n    log_blocks: Dict[int, str] = {}\n    try:\n        with open(file_path, 'r') as f:\n            for line_num, line in enumerate(f, 1):\n                if not line.strip(): continue # Skip empty lines\n                try:\n                    json_obj = json.loads(line)\n                    eval_id = json_obj.get('eval_id')\n                    log_content = json_obj.get('log_content') or json_obj.get('log') # 'log' for older format\n                    \n                    if eval_id is not None and log_content is not None:\n                        log_blocks[eval_id] = log_content\n                    else:\n                        print(f\"Warning: Line {line_num} in JSONL file missing 'eval_id' or 'log_content'/'log' field: {line.strip()[:100]}...\")\n                except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n                    print(f\"Warning: Failed to decode JSON from line {line_num}: {e}. Line: {line.strip()[:100]}...\"\
    )\n        return log_blocks\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"Error: JSONL log file not found at {file_path}.\")\n        return {}\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading JSONL logs: {e}\")\n        return {}\n\ndef extract_final_agent_strategies(log_content: str, agent_ids: List[str]) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the final action_strategy dictionary for each agent from a raw evaluation log string.\n    \n    Args:\n        log_content: The full string content of a single evaluation log block.\n        agent_ids: A list of agent IDs to look for (e.g., [\"Agent_1\", \"Agent_2\"]).\n    \n    Returns:\n        A dictionary mapping agent_id to their final action_strategy dictionary.\n        Returns an empty dict if no strategies are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    final_strategies: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    \n    for agent_id in agent_ids:\n        agent_id_escaped = re.escape(agent_id)\n        \n        # Pattern\
    \ to find the specific 'action_strategy = defaultdict' line associated with the agent.\n        # It captures the dictionary string after the defaultdict part.\n        # Using re.DOTALL to allow 'dot' to match newlines within the dictionary itself.\n        # ([\\s\\S]*?) for non-greedy match of the dictionary content.\n        strategy_line_pattern = r\"{agent_id_escaped} \\(Gen \\d+\\): Total Reward = [\\d.]+[\\s\\S]*?action_strategy = defaultdict\\(<function <lambda> at 0x[0-9a-fA-F]+>, (\\s*{{[\\s\\S]*?}})\\s*\\)\".format(agent_id_escaped=agent_id_escaped)\n\n        matches = list(re.finditer(strategy_line_pattern, log_content, re.DOTALL))\n        \n        if not matches:\n            # print(f\"Warning: No strategy lines found for {agent_id}.\")\n            continue\n            \n        last_match = matches[-1] # Get the last match, which should be the final strategy\n        strategy_str = last_match.group(1) # The captured group is the dict part\n        \n        # Sanitize\
    \ the string to be valid JSON\n        strategy_str = strategy_str.replace(\"'\", \"\\\"\")\n        strategy_str = re.sub(r\",(\\s*})\", r\"\\1\", strategy_str) # Remove trailing comma\n        \n        try:\n            strategy_dict = json.loads(strategy_str)\n            final_strategies[agent_id] = strategy_dict\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n            print(f\"Warning: Could not decode JSON strategy for {agent_id}: {e}\")\n            print(f\"  String: {strategy_str[:200]}...\")\n            \n    return final_strategies\n\ndef extract_general_info(log_content: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts general simulation info like generation, num_agents, num_rounds.\"\"\"\n    info = {}\n    \n    gen_match = re.search(r\"Generation (\\d+), Agents: (\\d+),\", log_content)\n    if gen_match:\n        info['generation_id'] = int(gen_match.group(1))\n        info['num_agents'] = int(gen_match.group(2))\n    \n    rounds_match = re.search(r\"Starting (\\d+) Rounds\
    \ of\", log_content)\n    if rounds_match:\n        info['num_rounds'] = int(rounds_match.group(1))\n        \n    return info\n\n# Example Usage (won't run in sandbox directly, but for local testing)\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    mock_jsonl_content = \"\"\"\n    {\"eval_id\": 437, \"log_content\": \"PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\\\\nSTDOUT:\\\\n...\\\\n  Agent_1 (Gen 1): Total Reward = 1000.0\\\\n    action_strategy = defaultdict(<function <lambda> at 0x...>, {'gather_wood': {'value_est': 0.8}, 'craft_foundation': {'value_est': 0.6}})\\\\n--- Simulation Complete (Generation 1)\\\"}\"\n    {\"eval_id\": 443, \"log_content\": \"PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\\\\nSTDOUT:\\\\n...\\\\n  Agent_1 (Gen 2): Total Reward = 1200.0\\\\n    action_strategy = defaultdict(<function <lambda> at 0x...>, {'gather_wood': {'value_est': 0.85}, 'craft_foundation': {'value_est': 0.7}})\\\\n--- Simulation Complete (Generation 2)\\\"}\"\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Mock load_jsonl_log_blocks\n    mock_log_blocks =\
    \ load_jsonl_log_blocks(\"non_existent_file.jsonl\") # Should report error\n    \n    # Simulate a manually parsed block for strategy extraction\n    sample_log_content_for_strategy = \"\"\"\n    PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n    STDOUT:\n    Executing command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n    --- Starting 2000 Rounds of Transgenerational Building Task (Generation 1, Agents: 5, Initial Complexity) ---\n      Agent_1 (Gen 1): Total Reward = 1170037.5\n        Specialization: Most=gather_wood, Index=0.32\n        Rep for Agent_2: 1.00\n        action_strategy = defaultdict(<function <lambda> at 0x...>, {'gather_wood': {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.8}, 'craft_foundation': {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.6}})\n    --- Simulation Complete (Generation 1) ---\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    mock_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(5)]\n    extracted_strategies = extract_final_agent_strategies(sample_log_content_for_strategy, mock_agent_ids)\n    \n\
    \    print(\"\\nExtracted Strategies (Mock Log for Strategy):\")\n    for agent_id, strategy in extracted_strategies.items():\n        print(f\"  {agent_id}: {json.dumps(strategy, indent=2)[:200]}...\")\n        \n    general_info = extract_general_info(sample_log_content_for_strategy)\n    print(\"\\nExtracted General Info (Mock Log for Strategy):\")\n    print(general_info)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
