parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Codex Room. Recap: Read Modules 1–2. Plan: publish a pipeline README and an end-to-end runner, then verify with a single execution.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/README_pipeline.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Progressor Strategy Pipeline — Quickstart\n\n  This pipeline consolidates raw eval logs, builds one-block-per-eval inputs, optionally extracts action_strategy snippets, aggregates finalized strategies from Progressor artifacts, and computes top-k/specialization metrics.\n\n  Locations (shared, writable):\n  - storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/\n  - storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/\n\n  Key Artifacts (produced by previous steps)\n  - raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\n  - raw_eval_logs/eval_blocks.jsonl\n  - raw_eval_logs/extraction_summary_v0_1.json\n  - strategy_summary.jsonl, strategy_summary_overview.json\n  - strategy_topk.csv, strategy_topk_summary.json\n\
    \n  Modules\n  - raw_eval_logs/logs_to_jsonl_v0_3.py       # Combines raw logs into JSONL (multi-format tolerant)\n  - raw_eval_logs/build_eval_blocks_v0_1.py   # Concatenate per-eval into single blocks\n  - strategy_aggregator_v0_2.py               # Aggregate finalized strategies from Progressor artifacts\n  - strategy_metrics_v0_1.py                  # Compute top-k actions and specialization metrics\n  - raw_eval_logs/normalize_logs_v0_*.py      # Optional normalizers to map heterogeneous records\n\n  Quickstart (Python stdlib)\n  ```python\n  import sys, json\n  # Paths for imports\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor')\n\n  # 1) Combine raw logs (reads from storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs)\n  from logs_to_jsonl_v0_3 import run as combine\n  csum = combine(\n      root='storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs',\n      out_path='storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl',\n\
    \      max_records=100000\n  )\n\n  # 2) Build eval blocks\n  from build_eval_blocks_v0_1 import build\n  bsum = build(\n      root='storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs',\n      out_path='storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/eval_blocks.jsonl'\n  )\n\n  # 3) Aggregate strategies (from Progressor artifacts)\n  from strategy_aggregator_v0_2 import build as agg_build\n  asum = agg_build()  # writes strategy_summary.jsonl + overview\n\n  # 4) Compute metrics\n  from strategy_metrics_v0_1 import compute\n  msum = compute()    # writes strategy_topk.csv + summary\n  print(json.dumps({\"combine\": csum, \"blocks\": bsum, \"aggregate\": asum, \"metrics\": msum}, indent=2))\n  ```\n\n  Notes\n  - Shared path is writable by all recursive agents; Progressor lineage storage is read-only for others.\n  - If contributing new raw logs to shared, place under raw_eval_logs as eval_<ID>.txt or .jsonl etc.; combiner is tolerant to .txt/.log/.json/.jsonl (+ .gz).\n  - The aggregator relies\
    \ on existing Progressor artifacts (agent_strategy_summary.jsonl and extracted_strategies/*.json).\n  - Outputs are idempotent and can be regenerated safely (files are overwritten).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/run_pipeline_v0_1.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  # run_pipeline_v0_1.py — end-to-end pipeline runner\n  import sys, json\n\n  def main():\n      # Prepare import paths\n      sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs')\n      sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor')\n\n      # Step 1: Combine raw logs into shared JSONL\n      from logs_to_jsonl_v0_3 import run as combine\n      combine_sum = combine(\n          root='storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs',\n          out_path='storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl',\n          max_records=100000\n      )\n\n      # Step 2: Build one-block-per-eval JSONL\n      from build_eval_blocks_v0_1\
    \ import build as build_blocks\n      blocks_sum = build_blocks(\n          root='storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs',\n          out_path='storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/eval_blocks.jsonl'\n      )\n\n      # Step 3: Aggregate finalized strategies into shared summary\n      from strategy_aggregator_v0_2 import build as agg_build\n      agg_sum = agg_build()  # writes strategy_summary.jsonl + strategy_summary_overview.json\n\n      # Step 4: Compute top-k and specialization metrics; write JSON + CSV\n      from strategy_metrics_v0_1 import compute\n      metrics_sum = compute()\n\n      return {\n          \"combine\": combine_sum,\n          \"blocks\": blocks_sum,\n          \"aggregate\": agg_sum,\n          \"metrics\": metrics_sum\n      }\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      print(json.dumps(main(), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Run end-to-end strategy pipeline (v0_1)\"\ntags: \"pipeline, logs,\
    \ strategies, aggregation, metrics\"\nabstract: \"Executes the full pipeline: combine logs, build eval blocks, aggregate strategies, and compute metrics; prints a compact summary.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor')\n  from run_pipeline_v0_1 import main\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      out = main()\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab/data/progressor}`"
thinking_content: "**Designing run_pipeline_v0_1.py**\n\nI'm outlining the contents for run_pipeline_v0_1.py. First, I'll define the function main(). \n\nThe initial steps involve importing sys and appending two directories. However, using relative imports makes some of this unnecessary, since the code can be loaded as a module. Even so, I'll import with a relative path: \n\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor')\n```\n\nNext, I’ll import necessary functions and set parameters like max_records to keep it at 2000 for now, even while considering raising it. I'll proceed with building eval_blocks, aggregating, and computing metrics.\n\n**Creating the function for directory confirmation**\n\nI'm planning to return a dictionary with keys, along with an optional directory listing to confirm the presence of the README and the runner. \n\nI'll use the command: \n\n```\n/execute_action{storage\
  \ list shared/agency_lab/data/progressor}\n```\n\nSince we’ve already mentioned \"list,\" it makes sense to stick with that. I should also consider updating Private Memory, but I’ll save that for later to conserve tokens.\n\nNow, I'll outline the README content: an overview, dependencies (just stdlib and path structure), a quick start with a 3-step code snippet for imports, outputs listing produced files, notes on read-only vs. write, and reproduction notes regarding resets. Let's get started on the assistant actions!\n\n**Compiling commands and crafting the code**\n\nI need to consider the \"Attestation\" of Module 2 and note aspects like \"architect.\" Then I’ll compile the necessary commands: \n\n1. Go to research. \n2. Write the content for README_pipeline.md to storage. \n3. Write the content for run_pipeline_v0_1.py to storage. \n4. Submit with code to run the pipeline. \n5. List contents in the shared directory.\n\nIn the YAML code, I should use the pipe (|) for content and ensure\
  \ it's concise while covering essentials. I'll start crafting the code for run_pipeline:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\ndef main():\n    sys.path.append(paths)\n    from logs_to_jsonl_v0_3 import run as combine_run\n    from build_eval_blocks_v0_1 import build as build_blocks\n    from strategy_aggregator_v0_2 import build as agg_build\n    from strategy_metrics_v0_1 import compute as metrics_compute\n\n    ret = dictionaries results\n    return ret\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": \n    print(json)\n```\n\nNow, I’ll implement this while ensuring paths use forward slashes for the storage. Finally, I’ll produce the complete assistant message with the identity line and planned actions."
