  **Finalizing YAML and pipeline setup**


  I need to ensure the YAML in the README properly includes any special characters, and the multi-line block looks fine. For the run_pipeline content, I''ll replicate what we had earlier. I also need to make sure the pipeline runner uses the correct function names and path injections we established. We have the logs and metrics set up in the right locations. Since the previous actions weren’t executed due to reading, I’ll perform them now while keeping the content concise and under the token limit. After submitting, I''ll check the results and list the directory to confirm success!


  **Preparing command execution**


  I need to include several commands for execution. First, I''ll use the command to go to research, followed by writing the README and run_pipeline files using previously established content. Then, I’ll submit the pipeline along with YAML for running the main code and finally list the directory. I have to be careful with backticks and follow the formatting instructions. After that, I will mention that we’re reissuing these actions due to previous suppression from codex reading. Let’s craft this efficiently!'
