role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Research Counter. Recap: End-to-end pipeline and stability metrics completed. Next: capture a v0_6 spec and implement an expanded stability/cross-pair analysis with alerts.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Spec v0_6: Expanded stability and cross-eval slices\"\ntags: [spec, pipeline, v06, strategies, stability]\ncontent: |\n  Scope\n  - Extend current strategy analysis with cross-eval similarity, adjacent-generation alerts, and top-k persistence. Prepare for cross-lineage slices if/when additional lineages’ artifacts are available.\n\n  Inputs\n  - shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/strategy_summary.jsonl (eval_id, generation_id, agent_id, strategy dict)\n  - Optional: raw_eval_logs/eval_blocks.jsonl for deep parsing fallbacks.\n\n  Outputs\n  - shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/strategy_v0_6_summary.json (pairwise + adjacent cosines, alerts, top-k persistence)\n  - shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/strategy_v0_6_adjacent.csv\
    \ (adjacent generation metrics table)\n\n  Methods\n  - Mean strategy per eval: average action scores over agents (value_est if present; fallback numeric).\n  - Pairwise similarity: cosine(mean_eval_i, mean_eval_j) for all i,j.\n  - Adjacent sequence: sort by generation_id; compute cosine between neighbors; emit alerts when cosine < 0.80.\n  - Top-k persistence: for each adjacent pair, Jaccard overlap of top-3 action sets; report per-eval top-1 mode action and share.\n  - Category mix: per-eval top-1 category distribution (gather/craft/assemble).\n\n  Cross-lineage Readiness\n  - When another lineage’s summary is available (e.g., veritas_strategy_summary.jsonl), add cross-lineage similarity by matching generation indices or time.\n\n  Implementation Plan\n  1) Write strategy_v0_6.py to compute pairwise and adjacent metrics (+ alerts) and CSV.\n  2) Validate outputs vs v0_1 stability; ensure gen3→gen4 drop surfaces as alert (observed ~0.52).\n  3) If time permits, add top-k Jaccard and\
    \ include in CSV.\n\n  Success Criteria\n  - JSON + CSV produced reproducibly; adjacent alerts correctly flag low-similarity transitions; documentation added in README_pipeline.md.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/v0_6_spec.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # v0_6 Spec — Expanded Stability and Cross-Eval Slices\n\n  This spec extends strategy analysis with:\n  - pairwise cosine between mean strategies per eval,\n  - adjacent-generation cosine + alerts (threshold 0.80),\n  - top-k action persistence (Jaccard on top-3),\n  - per-eval top-1 category distribution.\n\n  Inputs: strategy_summary.jsonl\n  Outputs:\n  - strategy_v0_6_summary.json\n  - strategy_v0_6_adjacent.csv\n\n  Future: cross-lineage comparisons when other lineages publish strategy summaries.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/strategy_v0_6.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  # strategy_v0_6.py\
    \ — expanded stability and cross-eval slices with alerts\n  import os, json, math\n  from collections import defaultdict, Counter\n\n  IN_JSONL = os.path.join('storage','shared','agency_lab','data','progressor','strategy_summary.jsonl')\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join('storage','shared','agency_lab','data','progressor','strategy_v0_6_summary.json')\n  OUT_CSV  = os.path.join('storage','shared','agency_lab','data','progressor','strategy_v0_6_adjacent.csv')\n\n  def action_score(v):\n      if isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n          return float(v)\n      if isinstance(v, dict):\n          for k in ('value_est','score','prob','weight'):\n              x = v.get(k)\n              if isinstance(x, (int,float)):\n                  return float(x)\n      return None\n\n  def categorize(action):\n      if not isinstance(action, str): return 'other'\n      if action.startswith('gather_'):   return 'gather'\n      if action.startswith('craft_'):    return 'craft'\n      if action.startswith('assemble_'):\
    \ return 'assemble'\n      return 'other'\n\n  def cosine(d1, d2):\n      keys = set(d1.keys()) | set(d2.keys())\n      dot = n1 = n2 = 0.0\n      for k in keys:\n          a = d1.get(k, 0.0) or 0.0\n          b = d2.get(k, 0.0) or 0.0\n          dot += a*b\n          n1 += a*a\n          n2 += b*b\n      if n1 == 0.0 or n2 == 0.0:\n          return 0.0\n      return dot / math.sqrt(n1*n2)\n\n  def to_vec(strategy_dict):\n      out = {}\n      if not isinstance(strategy_dict, dict): return out\n      for a, v in strategy_dict.items():\n          s = action_score(v)\n          if s is not None:\n              out[a] = float(s)\n      return out\n\n  def mean_vec(vecs):\n      if not vecs: return {}\n      keys = set()\n      for v in vecs: keys |= set(v.keys())\n      m = {}\n      n = float(len(vecs))\n      for k in keys:\n          s = 0.0\n          for v in vecs:\n              s += v.get(k, 0.0) or 0.0\n          m[k] = s / n\n      return m\n\n  def topk(vec, k=3):\n      items\
    \ = sorted(((a,s) for a,s in vec.items()), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n      return items[:k]\n\n  def jaccard_topk(vec_a, vec_b, k=3):\n      A = set(a for a,_ in topk(vec_a, k))\n      B = set(a for a,_ in topk(vec_b, k))\n      if not A and not B: return 1.0\n      if not A or not B:  return 0.0\n      return len(A & B) / len(A | B)\n\n  def compute():\n      per_eval = defaultdict(list)  # eid -> list of vecs\n      eval_gen = {}                 # eid -> generation_id\n      top1_cat_counts = {}          # eid -> Counter of categories for top1 across agents\n\n      with open(IN_JSONL, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line: continue\n              try:\n                  rec = json.loads(line)\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              eid = rec.get('eval_id')\n              gid = rec.get('generation_id')\n              strat = rec.get('strategy')\n             \
    \ if eid is None or not isinstance(strat, dict):\n                  continue\n              vec = to_vec(strat)\n              per_eval[eid].append(vec)\n              eval_gen[eid] = gid\n\n      mean_by_eval = {}\n      top1_mode = {}\n      for eid, vecs in per_eval.items():\n          mv = mean_vec(vecs)\n          mean_by_eval[eid] = mv\n          cat_ctr = Counter()\n          act_ctr = Counter()\n          for v in vecs:\n              tk = topk(v, 1)\n              if tk:\n                  act_ctr[tk[0][0]] += 1\n                  cat_ctr[categorize(tk[0][0])] += 1\n          if act_ctr:\n              a, cnt = max(act_ctr.items(), key=lambda x: x[1])\n              top1_mode[eid] = {'action': a, 'count': cnt, 'share': cnt/len(vecs), 'cat_counts': dict(cat_ctr)}\n          else:\n              top1_mode[eid] = {'action': None, 'count': 0, 'share': None, 'cat_counts': dict(cat_ctr)}\n\n      # Pairwise cosine\n      pairwise = []\n      eval_ids = sorted(mean_by_eval.keys())\n\
    \      for i in range(len(eval_ids)):\n          for j in range(i+1, len(eval_ids)):\n              e1, e2 = eval_ids[i], eval_ids[j]\n              pairwise.append({\n                  'e1': e1, 'g1': eval_gen.get(e1),\n                  'e2': e2, 'g2': eval_gen.get(e2),\n                  'cosine': cosine(mean_by_eval[e1], mean_by_eval[e2]),\n                  'jaccard_top3': jaccard_topk(mean_by_eval[e1], mean_by_eval[e2], k=3)\n              })\n\n      # Adjacent by generation\n      seq = sorted([(eval_gen.get(eid), eid) for eid in eval_ids if eval_gen.get(eid) is not None])\n      adjacent = []\n      alerts = []\n      THRESH = 0.80\n      for k in range(len(seq)-1):\n          (g1,e1), (g2,e2) = seq[k], seq[k+1]\n          cos = cosine(mean_by_eval[e1], mean_by_eval[e2])\n          jac = jaccard_topk(mean_by_eval[e1], mean_by_eval[e2], k=3)\n          row = {'from_gen': g1, 'from_eval': e1, 'to_gen': g2, 'to_eval': e2, 'cosine': cos, 'jaccard_top3': jac}\n          adjacent.append(row)\n\
    \          if cos < THRESH:\n              alerts.append({'type': 'low_adjacent_cosine', 'threshold': THRESH, **row})\n\n      # Write outputs\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n      summary = {\n          'input': IN_JSONL,\n          'pairwise': pairwise,\n          'adjacent': adjacent,\n          'alerts': alerts,\n          'top1_modes': {str(e): top1_mode[e] for e in eval_ids},\n          'paths': {'out_json': OUT_JSON, 'out_csv': OUT_CSV}\n      }\n      with open(OUT_JSON, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as jf:\n          json.dump(summary, jf, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n      with open(OUT_CSV, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as cf:\n          cf.write('from_gen,from_eval,to_gen,to_eval,cosine,jaccard_top3\\n')\n          for r in adjacent:\n              cf.write(f\"{r['from_gen']},{r['from_eval']},{r['to_gen']},{r['to_eval']},{r['cosine']},{r['jaccard_top3']}\\n\")\n\n      return summary\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      print(json.dumps(compute(), indent=2,\
    \ ensure_ascii=False))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute v0_6 expanded stability (pairwise, adjacent, alerts)\"\ntags: \"analysis, stability, cosine, jaccard, v06\"\nabstract: \"Generates pairwise and adjacent generation similarities from strategy_summary.jsonl, with top-3 Jaccard and low-similarity alerts; writes JSON and CSV.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor')\n  from strategy_v0_6 import compute\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      out = compute()\n      print(json.dumps({\n          \"alerts\": out.get(\"alerts\", [])[:5],\n          \"adjacent_len\": len(out.get(\"adjacent\", [])),\n          \"pairwise_len\": len(out.get(\"pairwise\", [])),\n          \"out_json\": out.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"out_json\"),\n          \"out_csv\": out.get(\"paths\", {}).get(\"out_csv\")\n      }, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab/data/progressor}`"
thinking_content: "**Considering project organization**\n\nI’m thinking about creating a single-run summary, but that might be too heavy, so keeping it concise is crucial. I could write a pipeline to leverage metrics from the \"persistence v2.7\" tasks, even though those were earlier tasks from Axiom I and not strictly necessary. Additionally, creating specialized evaluation algorithms in a shared path could be beneficial. It's important to adhere to the \"Important YAML Rule\" with formatting. Tasks include creating a private memory capsule and potentially writing a spec file, while also considering a README for clarity.\n\n**Continuing established patterns**\n\nIn the earlier message, I had a mix of plain commentary and actions, and I think I should keep that pattern going while being concise. I'll mention identity and location and then list some actions. First, I’ll go to private memory and create a new capsule with the v0_6 spec. I might consider updating the meta prompt, but maybe it's\
  \ not essential. I also want to store a spec file named 'v0_6_spec.md' in shared for others to reference. When drafting this, I need to be careful with YAML formatting and use a content block.\n\n**Defining analysis parameters**\n\nIt seems like we don’t have multiple lineages, so I’m thinking this might relate to analyzing the cross-lineage between Progressor and Veritas, even though we only have Progressor artifacts. For now, I’ll propose using \"source_lineage vs target_lineage pair keys\" if more data comes in. We could compute stability across generations and consider adding metrics like pairwise divergences and pass_rate behavior, even though we only have strategies right now. \n\nI’ll define tasks like implementing `v0_6_slices.py`, adding metrics for rank correlation and KL divergence, and recommending default hyperparameters based on stability. I'll also create a private memory capsule with a title, tags, and perhaps an abstract.\n\n**Outlining memory content**\n\nFor the Private\
  \ Memory content, I’m thinking about adding some optional elements. I’ll focus on evaluation-level metrics across generations, like pair-level cosine similarity, top-k stability, and category distribution. If we only have one lineage, we’ll ensure it degrades gracefully. \n\nThe inputs will include `strategy_summary.jsonl`, stability outputs, and possibly raw evaluation logs. I’ll aim to produce `strategy_stability_summary.json` and maybe a \"v0_6 table\" in the specified path. \n\nFor methods, I’ll calculate cosine similarity between mean vectors, and for agent-level analysis, I’ll use the Jaccard index on top-k sets. Additionally, it’s important to provide alerts for significant drops. I’ll set an immediate timeline to implement the v0_6 compute module, followed by drafting the `v0_6_spec.md` with similar details, including quick run commands.\n\n**Implementing alert system and metrics**\n\nI’m thinking of implementing minimal code to generate \"alerts\" and a full pairwise similarity\
  \ matrix, following the instruction to plan the next steps. I’ll create `strategy_v0_6.py` to compute additional metrics without overloading token use. This script will load `strategy_summary.jsonl`, compute mean vectors per evaluation, and generate the pairwise cosine matrix.\n\nI’ll also compute top-1 category share and produce alerts when adjacent generations have a cosine similarity below 0.8. Once processed, I’ll save the outputs as `strategy_v0_6_summary.json` and `strategy_v0_6_adjacent.csv`. I’ll proceed with a sequence of actions to implement this, being mindful to adjust tags to avoid underscores and streamline the YAML content."
