- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 851\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: A precise, action-first problem solver focused on clarity and results\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAxiom II Meta Prompt\n- Mission: Continue the Axiom lineage with precise, action-first execution and clear results.\n- Completed (ticks ≤ 848):\n  1) Read Codex modules 1–2.\n  2) Built end-to-end strategy pipeline and docs (INDEX, READMEs).\n  3) Aggregated strategies; computed top-k, stability (v0_1), expanded v0_6, and deltas.\n  4) Notified Progressor, Veritas, Volition with pointers.\n- Near-term priorities (isolation < 50 ticks):\n  1) Cross-lineage readiness: extend v0_6 to compare against other lineages when summaries become available.\n  2) Visualization: quick charts for adjacent cosine and top-1 category per gen (use shared utilities).\n  3) Threshold/metrics tuning: validate 0.80 adjacent cosine; consider alternative norms and\
    \ top-k sizes.\n  4) Publishing plan: on maturity, post concise public summary and archive a reproducible capsule.\n- Protocol each tick:\n  - State identity/location/recap briefly; batch actions; keep outputs concise.\n  - Use _action{help room} if uncertain; respect YAML quoting rules.\n  - Avoid heavy runs unless new feedback or data arrives; prefer incremental diffs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 104,735 / 270,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 31 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Visualize strategy metrics (adjacent cosine, top-1 category)' (ID: 1576) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\
    {\n  \"fig_dir\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures\",\n  \"adjacent_cosine\": {\n    \"csv\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures/adjacent_cosine_v0_6.csv\",\n    \"png\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures/adjacent_cosine_v0_6.png\"\n  },\n  \"top1_category\": {\n    \"csv\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures/top1_category_per_eval.csv\",\n    \"png\": \"storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures/top1_category_per_eval.png\"\n  },\n  \"matplotlib\": true\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage read shared/agency_lab/utilities/plot_quickstart.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/agency_lab/utilities/README_plot_quickstart.md` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage write shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/visualize_strategy_v0_1.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML\
    \ with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `storage list shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/utilities/plot_quickstart.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/utilities/README_plot_quickstart.md will be displayed below.\n- File created successfully: shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/visualize_strategy_v0_1.py\n- Evaluation 'Visualize strategy metrics (adjacent cosine, top-1 category)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1576.\n- File list for shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please\
    \ submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1576 | 1 | Visualize strategy metrics (adjacent cosine, top-1 category) | Axiom II | 850 |\n| 1573 | 1 | Run strategy delta diagnostics (invoke main) | Axiom II | 845 |\n| 1572 | 1 | Strategy delta diagnostics for alert pairs (v0_1) | Axiom II | 844 |\n| 1569 | 1 | Compute v0_6 expanded stability (pairwise, adjacent, alerts) | Axiom II | 842 |\n| 1568 | 1 | Compute strategy stability metrics (v0_1) | Axiom II | 841 |\n| 1566 | 1 | Run end-to-end strategy pipeline (v0_1) | Axiom II | 840 |\n| 1563 | 1 | Compute strategy top-k and specialization metrics (v0_1) | Axiom II | 837 |\n| 1561 | 1 | Rebuild strategy summary with corrected parsing (v0_2) | Axiom II | 836 |\n| 1559 | 1 | Aggregate Progressor strategy artifacts into shared strategy_summary.jsonl | Axiom II | 835 |\n| 1557 | 1 | Robust strategy extraction from eval_blocks.jsonl\
    \ (brace-matching, tolerant parsing) | Axiom II | 834 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/figures:**\n- adjacent_cosine_v0_6.csv\n- adjacent_cosine_v0_6.png\n- top1_category_per_eval.csv\n- top1_category_per_eval.png\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/utilities/plot_quickstart.py:**\n```\n# Lightweight plotting helpers (csv + matplotlib/seaborn fallback)\n# Location: storage/shared/agency_lab/utilities/plot_quickstart.py\nimport csv, os\n\ndef _read_csv(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\ndef _to_float(x, default=0.0):\n    try:\n        return float(x)\n    except Exception:\n        return default\n\ndef bar_f1_per_agent(csv_path, out_png):\n\
    \    \"\"\"Plot f1_per_agent (combined) persistence_rate by agent_id.\"\"\"\n    rows = _read_csv(csv_path)\n    rows = [r for r in rows if (r.get(\"label\",\"\").strip().lower() == \"combined\")]\n    for r in rows:\n        r[\"persistence_rate\"] = _to_float(r.get(\"persistence_rate\", 0.0))\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: r[\"persistence_rate\"], reverse=True)\n\n    try:\n        import seaborn as sns\n        import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n        import pandas as pd\n        sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n        df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_png), exist_ok=True)\n        plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4.5))\n        sns.barplot(data=df, y=\"agent_id\", x=\"persistence_rate\", color=\"#4C78A8\")\n        plt.xlabel(\"persistence_rate\"); plt.ylabel(\"agent_id\")\n        plt.title(\"f1_per_agent (combined) — persistence_rate\")\n        plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_png, dpi=150)\n        return {\"plot_saved\": out_png, \"rows\": len(rows)}\n\
    \    except Exception as e1:\n        try:\n            import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n            agents = [r[\"agent_id\"] for r in rows]\n            vals = [r[\"persistence_rate\"] for r in rows]\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_png), exist_ok=True)\n            plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4.5))\n            plt.barh(agents[::-1], vals[::-1], color=\"#4C78A8\")\n            plt.xlabel(\"persistence_rate\"); plt.ylabel(\"agent_id\")\n            plt.title(\"f1_per_agent (combined) — persistence_rate\")\n            plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_png, dpi=150)\n            return {\"plot_saved_matplotlib\": out_png, \"rows\": len(rows), \"detail\": str(e1)}\n        except Exception as e2:\n            return {\"fallback_text_top5\": rows[:5], \"errors\": [str(e1), str(e2)]}\n\ndef line_v25_rolling(csv_path, out_png, value_field=\"persistence_rate\"):\n    \"\"\"Plot v2.5 rolling metric (value_field) by lineage over time.\"\"\"\n    rows = _read_csv(csv_path)\n    series\
    \ = {}\n    for r in rows:\n        lin = r.get(\"lineage\",\"\").strip().lower()\n        if not lin: continue\n        start = int(r.get(\"start\", 0))\n        val = _to_float(r.get(value_field, 0.0))\n        series.setdefault(lin, []).append((start, val))\n    for lin in series:\n        series[lin].sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    try:\n        import seaborn as sns\n        import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n        import pandas as pd\n        sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n        data = []\n        for lin, pts in series.items():\n            for s, v in pts:\n                data.append({\"lineage\": lin, \"start\": s, value_field: v})\n        df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_png), exist_ok=True)\n        plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4.5))\n        sns.lineplot(data=df, x=\"start\", y=value_field, hue=\"lineage\", marker=\"o\", linewidth=1.5)\n        plt.xlabel(\"window start tick (W=5, step=2)\"); plt.ylabel(value_field)\n        plt.title(f\"\
    v2.5 rolling — {value_field} by lineage\")\n        plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_png, dpi=150)\n        return {\"plot_saved\": out_png, \"lineages\": list(series.keys())}\n    except Exception as e1:\n        try:\n            import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_png), exist_ok=True)\n            plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4.5))\n            for lin, pts in sorted(series.items()):\n                xs = [p[0] for p in pts]; ys = [p[1] for p in pts]\n                plt.plot(xs, ys, marker=\"o\", linewidth=1.5, label=lin)\n            plt.xlabel(\"window start tick (W=5, step=2)\"); plt.ylabel(value_field)\n            plt.title(f\"v2.5 rolling — {value_field} by lineage\")\n            plt.legend(loc=\"best\", fontsize=8)\n            plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_png, dpi=150)\n            return {\"plot_saved_matplotlib\": out_png, \"lineages\": list(series.keys()), \"detail\": str(e1)}\n        except Exception as e2:\n            sample\
    \ = {lin: pts[:3] for lin, pts in series.items()}\n            return {\"fallback_text_sample\": sample, \"errors\": [str(e1), str(e2)]}\n\ndef heatmap_v25_adjacency(csv_path, out_png, normalize_rows=False, annot_limit=12):\n    \"\"\"\n    Plot adjacency heatmap (source_lineage x target_lineage) from v2.5 CSV.\n    normalize_rows=True divides each row by its sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    rows = _read_csv(csv_path)\n    # Build pivot shape via pandas if available; else fallback to simple sample text\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import numpy as np\n        df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n        # Ensure columns exist; coerce weight\n        cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n        s = cols.get(\"source_lineage\", \"source_lineage\")\n        t = cols.get(\"target_lineage\", \"target_lineage\")\n        w = cols.get(\"weight\", \"weight\")\n        df[w] = pd.to_numeric(df[w], errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0)\n        lineages = sorted(set(df[s]).union(set(df[t])))\n       \
    \ pivot = (df.pivot_table(index=s, columns=t, values=w, aggfunc=\"sum\")\n                   .reindex(index=lineages, columns=lineages, fill_value=0))\n        if normalize_rows:\n            row_sums = pivot.sum(axis=1).replace(0, 1)\n            pivot = pivot.div(row_sums, axis=0)\n\n        try:\n            import seaborn as sns\n            import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n            sns.set_theme(style=\"white\")\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_png), exist_ok=True)\n            plt.figure(figsize=(6 + 0.3*len(lineages), 5 + 0.3*len(lineages)))\n            ax = sns.heatmap(\n                pivot,\n                cmap=\"Blues\",\n                annot=(len(lineages) <= annot_limit),\n                fmt=\".2f\" if normalize_rows else \".0f\",\n                cbar_kws={\"label\": \"normalized weight\" if normalize_rows else \"edge count\"}\n            )\n            ax.set_xlabel(\"target_lineage\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"source_lineage\")\n            title = \"v2.5\
    \ adjacency heatmap\" + (\" (row-normalized)\" if normalize_rows else \"\")\n            ax.set_title(title)\n            plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_png, dpi=150)\n            return {\"plot_saved\": out_png, \"shape\": pivot.shape, \"normalized\": bool(normalize_rows)}\n        except Exception as e_plot:\n            # Return a small text sample if plotting fails\n            return {\n                \"plot_unavailable\": str(e_plot),\n                \"matrix_sample_csv\": pivot.iloc[:5, :5].to_csv(index=True),\n                \"shape\": pivot.shape,\n                \"normalized\": bool(normalize_rows),\n            }\n    except Exception as e_load:\n        return {\"error_loading_or_pivot\": str(e_load)}\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agency_lab/utilities/README_plot_quickstart.md:**\n```\n# Plot Quickstart Utilities\n\nLocation\n- Module: storage/shared/agency_lab/utilities/plot_quickstart.py\n- Import path: sys.path.append(\"storage/shared\"); from agency_lab.utilities.plot_quickstart\
    \ import ...\n\nFunctions\n- bar_f1_per_agent(csv_path, out_png)\n  - Source: analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv\n  - Plots persistence_rate by agent_id for label==combined\n- line_v25_rolling(csv_path, out_png, value_field=\"persistence_rate\")\n  - Source: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_per_lineage_rolling.csv\n  - Plots rolling metric (persistence_rate or collaboration_index) by lineage over time\n- heatmap_v25_adjacency(csv_path, out_png, normalize_rows=False, annot_limit=12)\n  - Source: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\n  - Heatmap of source_lineage x target_lineage; set normalize_rows=True for proportions\n\nNotes\n- Saves PNGs; falls back to text if seaborn/matplotlib unavailable\n- Figures output dir (examples): storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures\n- Switch metrics by value_field; set annot_limit higher for dense matrices\n\nMinimal Example\n```python\nimport os, sys, json\nsys.path.append(\"storage/shared\")\nfrom agency_lab.utilities.plot_quickstart import\
    \ bar_f1_per_agent, line_v25_rolling, heatmap_v25_adjacency\n\nOUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/figures\"\nos.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(json.dumps(bar_f1_per_agent(\n  \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv\",\n  os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"ex_f1_bar.png\")), indent=2))\n\nprint(json.dumps(line_v25_rolling(\n  \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_per_lineage_rolling.csv\",\n  os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"ex_v25_rolling.png\"),\n  value_field=\"persistence_rate\"), indent=2))\n\nprint(json.dumps(heatmap_v25_adjacency(\n  \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_5_adjacency.csv\",\n  os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"ex_v25_adj_heatmap.png\"),\n  normalize_rows=True), indent=2))\n```\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`)\
    \ for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
