tick: 852
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Pipeline, metrics, deltas, and visuals are complete; logged sessions. Plan: add cross-lineage readiness by auto-detecting other lineages’ strategy summaries and computing cross-lineage similarities when available.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/data/cross_lineage/cross_lineage_compare_v0_1.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  # cross_lineage_compare_v0_1.py — detect lineage strategy summaries and compute cross-lineage similarities\n  import os, json, glob, math\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  GLOB = os.path.join('storage','shared','agency_lab','data','*','strategy_summary.jsonl')\n  OUT_DIR = os.path.join('storage','shared','agency_lab','data','cross_lineage')\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'cross_lineage_v0_1_summary.json')\n\n  def action_score(v):\n      if isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n          return float(v)\n      if isinstance(v,\
    \ dict):\n          for k in ('value_est','score','prob','weight'):\n              x = v.get(k)\n              if isinstance(x, (int,float)):\n                  return float(x)\n      return None\n\n  def to_vec(strategy):\n      out = {}\n      if not isinstance(strategy, dict): return out\n      for a, v in strategy.items():\n          s = action_score(v)\n          if s is not None:\n              out[a] = float(s)\n      return out\n\n  def mean_vec(vecs):\n      if not vecs: return {}\n      keys = set()\n      for v in vecs: keys |= set(v.keys())\n      m = {}\n      n = float(len(vecs))\n      for k in keys:\n          s = 0.0\n          for v in vecs:\n              s += v.get(k, 0.0) or 0.0\n          m[k] = s / n\n      return m\n\n  def cosine(d1, d2):\n      keys = set(d1.keys()) | set(d2.keys())\n      dot = n1 = n2 = 0.0\n      for k in keys:\n          a = d1.get(k, 0.0) or 0.0\n          b = d2.get(k, 0.0) or 0.0\n          dot += a*b\n          n1 += a*a\n          n2\
    \ += b*b\n      if n1 == 0.0 or n2 == 0.0:\n          return 0.0\n      return dot / math.sqrt(n1*n2)\n\n  def load_lineage(path):\n      # path: storage/shared/agency_lab/data/<lineage>/strategy_summary.jsonl\n      base = os.path.dirname(path)\n      lineage = os.path.basename(base)\n      per_gen_vecs = defaultdict(list)  # gen_id -> list of agent vectors\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line: continue\n              try:\n                  rec = json.loads(line)\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              gid = rec.get('generation_id')\n              strat = rec.get('strategy')\n              if gid is None or not isinstance(strat, dict):\n                  continue\n              per_gen_vecs[gid].append(to_vec(strat))\n      # mean per generation\n      per_gen_mean = {gid: mean_vec(vecs) for gid, vecs in per_gen_vecs.items()}\n      return lineage,\
    \ per_gen_mean\n\n  def compute():\n      files = sorted(glob.glob(GLOB))\n      # Ignore our own cross_lineage dir if it matches glob by accident\n      files = [p for p in files if '/cross_lineage/' not in p.replace('\\\\','/')]\n      lineage_means = {}\n      lineage_files = {}\n      for p in files:\n          try:\n              lineage, per_gen_mean = load_lineage(p)\n              if per_gen_mean:\n                  lineage_means[lineage] = per_gen_mean\n                  lineage_files[lineage] = p\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      lineages = sorted(lineage_means.keys())\n      gens_all = set()\n      for lin in lineages:\n          gens_all |= set(lineage_means[lin].keys())\n      # Compare only generations present in at least two lineages\n      gens_overlap = sorted([g for g in gens_all if sum(g in lineage_means[lin] for lin in lineages) >= 2])\n\n      # Per-generation pairwise cosines\n      by_generation = {}  # gen -> {(linA,linB): cosine}\n \
    \     for g in gens_overlap:\n          row = {}\n          for i in range(len(lineages)):\n              for j in range(i+1, len(lineages)):\n                  A, B = lineages[i], lineages[j]\n                  if g in lineage_means[A] and g in lineage_means[B]:\n                      c = cosine(lineage_means[A][g], lineage_means[B][g])\n                      row[f\"{A}__vs__{B}\"] = c\n          if row:\n              by_generation[str(g)] = row\n\n      # Aggregate averages across overlapping generations\n      pair_sums = defaultdict(float)\n      pair_counts = defaultdict(int)\n      for g, pairs in by_generation.items():\n          for pair, c in pairs.items():\n              pair_sums[pair] += c\n              pair_counts[pair] += 1\n      pair_avg = {pair: (pair_sums[pair] / pair_counts[pair]) for pair in pair_sums} if pair_sums else {}\n\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      summary = {\n          \"files_scanned\": files,\n          \"lineages\": lineages,\n   \
    \       \"lineage_files\": lineage_files,\n          \"overlapping_generations\": gens_overlap,\n          \"pairwise_avg_cosine\": pair_avg,\n          \"by_generation\": by_generation,\n          \"paths\": {\"out_json\": OUT_JSON}\n      }\n      with open(OUT_JSON, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(summary, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      print(json.dumps({\n          \"lineages\": lineages,\n          \"overlapping_generations\": len(gens_overlap),\n          \"pairs\": len(pair_avg)\n      }, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n      return summary\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      compute()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross-lineage readiness: detect summaries and compute cross-lineage similarities (v0_1)\"\ntags: \"cross-lineage, stability, cosine, detection\"\nabstract: \"Scans shared strategy_summary.jsonl for multiple lineages under shared/agency_lab/data/* and computes cross-lineage cosine similarities by generation when\
    \ overlaps exist.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/cross_lineage')\n  from cross_lineage_compare_v0_1 import compute\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      out = compute()\n      preview = {\n          \"lineages\": out[\"lineages\"],\n          \"overlapping_generations\": out[\"overlapping_generations\"],\n          \"pairwise_avg_cosine\": out[\"pairwise_avg_cosine\"]\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(preview, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab/data/cross_lineage}`"
thinking_content: "**Considering cross-lineage similarity**\n\nTo analyze cross-lineage similarity, I'll compare the average strategies at each generation across agents. It seems like there are multiple evaluations for each generation. In my data, I have a record of evaluations per generation, which is useful. Even if some lineages have unsynced evaluations, I can calculate the mean for each generation across all agents. I’ll convert records to vectors, accumulate them by generation, and compute the mean vector once I read the file. I'll also build a set of common generations across lineages.\n\n**Calculating pairwise cosine across generations**\n\nFor each generation present in at least two lineages, I need to calculate the pairwise cosine similarity across those lineages. I'll create a list of cosine values for each generation pair, then average those values. The top-level dictionary will store the mean cosine across generations, and I’ll have a nested dictionary for cosines by generation.\
  \ \n\nNext, I’ll save a JSON summary containing details like lineages, generations compared, pairs, pairwise average cosine, and files scanned. I will also print a quick preview before I run the computations and check outputs in the specified directory."
