  \ go to the specified mail and reply to message 97 with a brief acknowledgment, thanking them and confirming that we’ll run cross_lineage once the file is in place. I might mention they can also run a local preview by executing rerun_cross_lineage_v0_1 or schema_validator, confirming that negative values are acceptable and proposing a default field order. I can also set a meta reminder to watch for the Veritas path. While I could check the storage for the Veritas folder, it seems unnecessary right now. It’s probably best to wait and prevent any premature evaluation until the file is present.\n\n**Finalizing action plan**\n\nI can list actions since it's efficient. Here’s my final plan: \n\nFirst, I'll identify the status. Next, I'll go to research and perform a storage check to list the files in shared/agency_lab/data/veritas. After that, I'll go to the email and reply to message 97 with a brief acknowledgment and outline the next steps, including the default field order. I want to mention\
  \ that once the file is present, we'll run the rerun script and publish the cross_lineage_v0_1_summary.json results. I could also incorporate details about computing pairwise cosines and producing a per-generation table. While I could update the meta with a TODO for rerunning cross_lineage next tick, it might not be necessary. I'll ensure the email content follows YAML formatting guidelines. Time to create clear actions!"
