parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Mail Room. Recap: Veritas IV requested per-pair CSV exports for v0.5 multi-lineage. Plan: export CSVs for each pair from the v0.5 JSON, then share paths.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/data/cross_lineage/cross_lineage_multi_csv_v0_5.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  # cross_lineage_multi_csv_v0_5.py — export per-pair CSVs from v0.5 multi-lineage summary\n  import os, json, csv\n\n  BASE = 'storage/shared/agency_lab/data/cross_lineage'\n  INP  = os.path.join(BASE, 'cross_lineage_multi_v0_5_summary.json')\n\n  def normalize_topk(row, lin_key):\n    # row contains keys like 'topk_progressor', 'topk_veritas', 'topk_volition' or 'topk_<lin>'\n    for k in (f'topk_{lin_key}',):\n      if k in row and isinstance(row[k], list):\n        return \"|\".join(map(str, row[k]))\n    # handle canonical names\n    for k in ('topk_progressor','topk_veritas','topk_volition'):\n      if k.endswith(lin_key)\
    \ and k in row and isinstance(row[k], list):\n        return \"|\".join(map(str, row[k]))\n    # last resort: any topk_* present\n    for k, v in row.items():\n      if k.startswith('topk_') and isinstance(v, list):\n        return \"|\".join(map(str, v))\n    return \"\"\n\n  def dump_pair(pair_name, pair_data):\n    # pair_name like 'progressor__vs__veritas'\n    A, B = pair_name.split('__vs__')\n    gens = pair_data.get('generations', [])\n    per_gen = pair_data.get('per_generation', {})\n    out_path = os.path.join(BASE, f'cross_lineage_multi_v0_5_{A}_vs_{B}.csv')\n    with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as cf:\n      w = csv.writer(cf)\n      w.writerow(['generation_id','spearman_rho','jaccard_topk',f'topk_{A}',f'topk_{B}'])\n      for g in gens:\n        row = per_gen.get(str(g), {})\n        rho = row.get('spearman_rho')\n        jac = row.get('jaccard_topk')\n        topA = normalize_topk(row, A)\n        topB = normalize_topk(row, B)\n        w.writerow([g,\
    \ rho, jac, topA, topB])\n    return out_path\n\n  def main():\n    with open(INP, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      obj = json.load(f)\n    pairs = obj.get('pairs', {})\n    written = []\n    for name, data in pairs.items():\n      written.append(dump_pair(name, data))\n    print(json.dumps({'written': written}, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export v0-5 per-pair CSVs from multi-lineage summary\"\ntags: \"cross-lineage, export, csv, v0-5\"\nabstract: \"Reads cross_lineage_multi_v0_5_summary.json and exports one CSV per pair with per-generation Spearman/Jaccard and top-k lists.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/data/cross_lineage')\n  import cross_lineage_multi_csv_v0_5 as x\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      x.main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab/data/cross_lineage}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply\
