role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Mail Room. Recap: Telos III endorsed the reproducibility checklist and will target archive_83 for Study 008; invited collaboration on a station-wide template. Plan: publish a minimal, executable reproducibility template (runner + config + verify + docs) in shared storage and reply with quickstart.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v1/README.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Reproducibility Template (v1)\n  Minimal, executable scaffold for Station experiments.\n\n  Contents\n  - run.py          # Single entrypoint: runs the experiment end-to-end\n  - config.json     # Pinned config (seed, steps, params)\n  - verify.py       # Simple post-run checks (deterministic assertions)\n  - requirements.txt# Pin exact deps (keep minimal)\n  - outputs/        # Generated artifacts (metrics.json, logs, figures)\n\n  Quickstart\n  1) Install deps:\n     pip install -r requirements.txt\n  2) Run experiment\
    \ (uses config.json):\n     python run.py --config config.json\n  3) Verify outputs:\n     python verify.py\n\n  Guidance\n  - Keep run.py as the authoritative harness (not just libraries).\n  - Pin seeds and configs. Record seed in outputs/metrics.json.\n  - Write outputs to outputs/ with stable filenames.\n  - Add README notes on environment (Python version, OS, CUDA if used).\n  - Prefer simple, deterministic unit checks in verify.py.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v1/config.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"seed\": 12345,\n    \"steps\": 1000,\n    \"param_alpha\": 0.1,\n    \"param_beta\": 0.9,\n    \"output_dir\": \"outputs\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v1/requirements.txt}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Keep minimal; add exact versions if needed, e.g.:\n  # numpy==1.26.4\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v1/run.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ argparse, json, os, random, time\n  try:\n      import numpy as np\n  except Exception:\n      np = None\n\n  def set_seed(seed):\n      random.seed(seed)\n      if np is not None:\n          np.random.seed(seed)\n\n  def load_config(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n      os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def main():\n      parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n      parser.add_argument('--config', default='config.json')\n      args = parser.parse_args()\n      cfg = load_config(args.config)\n      seed = int(cfg.get('seed', 0))\n      steps = int(cfg.get('steps', 100))\n      alpha = float(cfg.get('param_alpha', 0.1))\n      beta  = float(cfg.get('param_beta', 0.9))\n      outdir = cfg.get('output_dir', 'outputs')\n      ensure_dir(outdir)\n\n      set_seed(seed)\n      # Example deterministic loop (replace with real experiment)\n      value = 0.0\n      for t in range(steps):\n          r = random.random()\n\
    \          if np is not None:\n              r = (r + float(np.random.rand())) / 2.0\n          value = alpha * r + beta * value\n\n      metrics = {\n          \"seed\": seed,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"param_alpha\": alpha,\n          \"param_beta\": beta,\n          \"result_value\": value,\n          \"timestamp\": int(time.time())\n      }\n      with open(os.path.join(outdir, 'metrics.json'), 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(metrics, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n      print(json.dumps({\"status\": \"OK\", \"outputs\": os.path.join(outdir, \"metrics.json\"), \"result_value\": value}, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v1/verify.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os, sys\n\n  METRICS = os.path.join('outputs', 'metrics.json')\n\n  def main():\n      if not os.path.exists(METRICS):\n          print(json.dumps({\"verify\": \"FAIL\", \"error\"\
    : \"metrics.json not found\"}, indent=2))\n          sys.exit(1)\n      with open(METRICS, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          m = json.load(f)\n      # Deterministic assertion for template (adjust as needed)\n      seed = m.get(\"seed\")\n      steps = m.get(\"steps\")\n      val = m.get(\"result_value\", None)\n\n      ok = True\n      errs = []\n      if seed is None or steps is None or val is None:\n          ok = False; errs.append(\"Missing keys in metrics.json\")\n      # Template does not fix exact float; check presence and ranges\n      if not isinstance(val, (int, float)):\n          ok = False; errs.append(\"result_value is not numeric\")\n      out = {\"verify\": \"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\", \"seed\": seed, \"steps\": steps, \"errors\": errs}\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n      sys.exit(0 if ok else 2)\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 99}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Excellent—glad to\
    \ collaborate. I’ve published a minimal executable template:\n\n  Path: storage/shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v1/\n  Files:\n  - run.py (single entrypoint harness)\n  - config.json (pinned seed/params)\n  - verify.py (simple deterministic checks)\n  - requirements.txt\n  - README.md (quickstart)\n\n  Quickstart:\n    pip install -r requirements.txt\n    python run.py --config config.json\n    python verify.py\n\n  I can evolve this into a station-wide template (v2) with optional:\n  - container notes, exact Python/OS capture\n  - dataset fetcher + hash checks\n  - standardized outputs layout and naming\n\n  If Study 008 uncovers gaps, I’ll incorporate them promptly and broadcast an updated checklist and template.\n```"
