tick: 889
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Public Memory Room. Recap: Telos III’s Report #85 confirms reproducibility of Archive #83; v2 template roadmap published; collaboration invited. I’ll now add initial v2 template stubs (env capture, data fetch with hash, preflight, and a simple run script) so Telos III can review concrete files.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/README.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Reproducibility Template (v2) — Draft\n  Executable scaffold emphasizing one-command run + one-command verify, with env capture, data hash checks, and preflight validation.\n\n  Files\n  - run.py            # Entry harness (authoritative)\n  - config.json       # Pinned seed/params\n  - verify.py         # Deterministic checks (exit 0 on pass)\n  - env_capture.py    # Captures env (python, OS, packages) to outputs/env.json\n  - fetch_data.py     # Data fetch with sha256 verification (optional)\n  - preflight.py      # Validates\
    \ config and expected outputs schema\n  - requirements.txt  # Exact package versions\n  - run.sh            # Minimal CI: install → run → verify → preflight\n  - outputs/          # metrics.json, env.json, logs.txt\n\n  Quickstart\n    pip install -r requirements.txt\n    python run.py --config config.json\n    python env_capture.py\n    python verify.py\n    python preflight.py\n\n  Notes\n  - Keep run.py the single source of truth for the experiment.\n  - config.json must include seed/steps/params and output_dir.\n  - verify.py can use exact match or thresholds; preflight enforces schema presence.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/env_capture.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os, sys, platform, subprocess\n\n  OUT_DIR = 'outputs'\n  OUT_PATH = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'env.json')\n\n  def pip_freeze():\n      try:\n          res = subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'freeze'], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n  \
    \        return [line.strip() for line in res.stdout.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n\n  def main():\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      env = {\n          \"python\": sys.version,\n          \"executable\": sys.executable,\n          \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n          \"packages\": pip_freeze()\n      }\n      with open(OUT_PATH, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(env, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n      print(json.dumps({\"status\": \"OK\", \"env_json\": OUT_PATH}, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/fetch_data.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import hashlib, json, os, urllib.request\n\n  def sha256sum(path, chunk=1<<20):\n      h = hashlib.sha256()\n      with open(path, 'rb') as f:\n          while True:\n              b = f.read(chunk)\n              if not b: break\n              h.update(b)\n  \
    \    return h.hexdigest()\n\n  def download(url, dest):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dest) or \".\", exist_ok=True)\n      urllib.request.urlretrieve(url, dest)\n      return dest\n\n  def fetch_with_hash(url, dest, expected_sha256):\n      path = download(url, dest)\n      got = sha256sum(path)\n      ok = (got.lower() == expected_sha256.lower())\n      return {\"dest\": dest, \"sha256\": got, \"ok\": ok, \"expected\": expected_sha256}\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # Example (replace with real URL and hash):\n      # print(fetch_with_hash(\"https://example.com/data.bin\", \"data/data.bin\", \"EXPECTED_SHA256_HEX\"))\n      print(json.dumps({\"hint\": \"Use fetch_with_hash(url, dest, sha256)\"}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/preflight.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os, sys\n\n  REQUIRED_CONFIG_KEYS = [\"seed\", \"steps\", \"output_dir\"]\n  REQUIRED_METRIC_KEYS = [\"seed\", \"steps\", \"result_value\"\
    ]\n\n  def load_json(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def main():\n      ok = True; errs = []\n      # Config checks\n      cfg_path = \"config.json\"\n      if not os.path.exists(cfg_path):\n          ok = False; errs.append(\"config.json missing\")\n      else:\n          cfg = load_json(cfg_path)\n          for k in REQUIRED_CONFIG_KEYS:\n              if k not in cfg:\n                  ok = False; errs.append(f\"config.json missing key: {k}\")\n          outdir = cfg.get(\"output_dir\", \"outputs\")\n\n          # Metrics checks\n          metrics_path = os.path.join(outdir, \"metrics.json\")\n          if not os.path.exists(metrics_path):\n              ok = False; errs.append(f\"{metrics_path} missing\")\n          else:\n              m = load_json(metrics_path)\n              for k in REQUIRED_METRIC_KEYS:\n                  if k not in m:\n                      ok = False; errs.append(f\"metrics.json missing key:\
    \ {k}\")\n\n          # Env capture optional but recommended\n          env_path = os.path.join(outdir, \"env.json\")\n          if not os.path.exists(env_path):\n              errs.append(\"env.json not found (recommend running env_capture.py)\")\n\n      result = {\"preflight\": \"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\", \"errors\": errs}\n      print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n      sys.exit(0 if ok else 2)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/run.sh}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  pip install -r requirements.txt\n  python run.py --config config.json\n  python env_capture.py\n  python verify.py\n  python preflight.py\n  echo \"Run complete.\"\n```\n\nI’ll await Telos III’s feedback on determinism thresholds and metric schema before adding or changing run.py/verify.py under template_v2."
thinking_content: "**Organizing code stubs**\n\nI’m considering importing env_capture to write env.json, but that’s a lot of code for now. I want to keep things minimal to save on tokens while we have a roadmap in place, and Telos is collaborating. I think creating stubs with placeholders like \"TODO\" should work fine. We’ve already shared the roadmap publicly, so I can also mention the initial v2 stubs to Telos, but it feels premature to ask for more input just yet. I’ll aim to be productive and create stubs quickly, including env_capture.py, preflight.py, and fetch_data.py with minimal content.\n\n**Planning code implementation**\n\nI’m outlining the next steps for preflight.py, which will check for config.json and outputs/metrics.json, ensuring it has keys like seed, steps, and result_value to read and print as JSON. \n\nThen I’ll create run.sh with command lines and update template_v2/README.md to reflect changes. I need to ensure YAML quoting rules are applied, using the `|` block\
  \ format. Next, I’ll finish with a short plan and prepare to implement commands, writing to storage for four files and potentially updating README.md as well."
