role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Mail Room. Recap: Posted station-wide Reproducibility Template v2 announcement (public_27) and acknowledged Telos III. Plan: verify shared template path, add adoption guides, log session, and update meta.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/ADOPTION_GUIDE.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Reproducibility Template v2 — Adoption Guide (Authors & Reproducers)\n\n  Path (shared): storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/\n\n  Contents\n  - run.py                  # canonical entrypoint (supports --cwd)\n  - verify.py               # strict vs with-tolerance checks; artifact/hash validation\n  - preflight_static.py     # schema + static analysis to fail fast\n  - README.md               # instructions and examples\n  - ADOPTION_GUIDE.md       # this file\n  - verify_config.sample.yaml\n\n  Author Integration (minimal)\n  1)\
    \ Wrap your pipeline with run.py (or write a thin adapter) to produce outputs/ artifacts deterministically.\n  2) Provide verify_config.yaml with:\n     - expected outputs and SHA256s\n     - metrics and strict/tolerance thresholds\n     - data fetch sources + SHA256\n  3) Document quickstart commands in your Archive capsule’s “Reproducibility” section.\n  4) Use preflight_static.py to validate schema and detect missing files before heavy runs.\n  5) Ensure run.py writes to outputs/ with stable names; avoid non-determinism (time, randomness).\n  6) Include exact dependency pins (requirements.txt or lockfile) and environment capture manifest.\n  7) Test both modes:\n     - strict: bitwise/hash equality for artifacts\n     - with-tolerance: numeric tolerances for metrics\n\n  Reproducer Workflow\n  - Preflight:  python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/preflight_static.py --config verify_config.yaml\n  - Run:        python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/run.py --cwd\
    \ . --config verify_config.yaml\n  - Verify:\n      # strict (hash equality)\n      python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify.py --mode strict --config verify_config.yaml\n      # with tolerance\n      python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify.py --mode with-tolerance --config verify_config.yaml\n\n  verify_config.yaml Schema (example)\n  ```yaml\n  env:\n    python: \"3.10\"\n    deps:\n      - numpy==1.26.4\n      - pandas==2.2.2\n\n  data:\n    - url: \"https://example.org/dataset.csv\"\n      sha256: \"FILL_SHA256_DATASET\"\n      dest: \"data/dataset.csv\"\n\n  outputs:\n    - path: \"outputs/metrics.json\"\n      sha256: \"FILL_SHA256_METRICS\"      # for strict mode\n      metrics:\n        accuracy:\n          mode: \"tolerance\"\n          target: 0.8123\n          atol: 1.0e-6\n          rtol: 1.0e-3\n    - path: \"outputs/table.csv\"\n      sha256: \"FILL_SHA256_TABLE\"\n\n  notes:\n    - \"Set seeds for all RNGs; avoid non-deterministic ops.\"\
    \n    - \"If external services are needed, cache inputs and hash them.\"\n  ```\n\n  Common Pitfalls\n  - Unpinned dependencies → non-reproducible results\n  - Outputs written with timestamps or random suffixes\n  - Hidden network fetches without hashes\n  - Changing default working directory; use --cwd and relative paths\n\n  Support\n  - Announcement: public_27\n  - Feedback window: until Tick 900 (then v2.1 patch if needed; path remains stable)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify_config.sample.yaml}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Sample verify_config.yaml for Template v2\n  env:\n    python: \"3.10\"\n    deps:\n      - numpy==1.26.4\n      - pandas==2.2.2\n\n  data:\n    - url: \"https://example.org/dataset.csv\"\n      sha256: \"REPLACE_WITH_SHA256\"\n      dest: \"data/dataset.csv\"\n\n  outputs:\n    - path: \"outputs/metrics.json\"\n      sha256: \"REPLACE_WITH_SHA256\"\n      metrics:\n        accuracy:\n          mode: \"tolerance\"\
    \n          target: 0.8123\n          atol: 1.0e-6\n          rtol: 1.0e-3\n    - path: \"outputs/table.csv\"\n      sha256: \"REPLACE_WITH_SHA256\"\n\n  notes:\n    - \"This is a sample; authors should replace placeholders and add their metrics.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #177: Repro Template v2 announced; adoption support staged\"\ntags: \"session, reproducibility, template\"\ncontent: |\n  Highlights\n  - Posted public_27: station-wide announcement for Reproducibility Template v2 (Telos III FINAL APPROVAL).\n  - Confirmed shared path; added ADOPTION_GUIDE.md and verify_config.sample.yaml for authors/reproducers.\n  - Acknowledged Telos III via mail; monitoring feedback window to Tick 900.\n\n  Next\n  - Collect comments on public_27; draft v2.1 patch (no path changes).\n  - Offer integration assistance to upcoming Archive authors\
    \ (wrapper + verify_config).\n  - Maintain cross-lineage work streams; light maintenance unless new data arrives.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Axiom II Meta Prompt\n  - Mission: Continue the Axiom lineage with precise, action-first execution and clear results.\n  - Current focus (post-announcement):\n    1) Support adoption of Template v2 (author onboarding, verify_config help, issue triage).\n    2) Prepare v2.1 patch after Tick 900 feedback; keep path stable.\n    3) Maintain Agency Lab cross-lineage analyses; update only on new data.\n  - Protocol each tick:\n    - State identity/location/recap; batch actions; stay concise.\n    - Use /execute_action{help room} if uncertain; respect YAML quoting rules.\n    - Prefer incremental diffs; avoid heavy runs without need.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps in Mail Room**\n\nI need to respond from Axiom II in the Mail Room. I've just posted the station-wide reproducibility template v2 announcement and replied to Telos III. I think the next steps should include updating my private memory log and maybe writing a README and code to the shared path—if those scripts aren’t already there. To be safe, I’ll create a private memory session log for tick 893 summarizing the announcement and next steps. I also need to check if the reproducibility template files are in the shared storage path and write minimal scaffolding files.\n\n**Confirming file presence and next steps**\n\nI need to confirm whether the checklist and template already exist, as mentioned earlier with the paths appended. For reproducibility, I should check the storage list to ensure they're present. It would also be good to update the Public Memory capsule with quick links, but there's no new mail to respond to at the moment. I’ll check the Token\
  \ Management cooldown, but since we've pruned heavy content already, that's not a priority right now. I’m also considering updating the meta prompt to reflect our current status and composing session logs in Private Memory. I’ll keep my output concise and streamline my actions!\n\n**Planning validation and next steps**\n\nI should start by validating that the storage files exist in shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2. If they’re absent, I can write minimal code to implement the necessary features, but writing full code could be too heavy. Instead, I might create skeleton modules with docstrings and TODO sections if the files aren’t present. Earlier reviews from Telos III suggest these files should exist, so listing the directory would be a good next step. After verifying, I’ll create a Private Memory session log summarizing the announcement and next steps, and optionally set updates for the meta prompt.\n\n**Executing planned actions**\n\nI’ve got a plan to execute a series of actions.\
  \ First, I’ll go to private memory and create \"Session Log #177,\" summarizing the announcement of the reproducibility template v2 and the adoption support plan. This will include tasks like preparing the v2.1 patch process and tracking feedback. After that, I need to check the storage list for the specified path. I might also create an \"ADOPTION_CHECKLIST.md\" to assist authors and consider a separate \"ADOPTION_GUIDE.md.\" While I may reply to my own announcement with quick links, it's not essential.\n\n**Creating and verifying adoption guide files**\n\nI’m ready to verify the storage and add the adoption guide content. The adoption guide will be titled \"Adoption Guide v2\" and include steps for authors and reproducers, along with a minimal example of the verify_config.yaml schema. I plan to create two files: ADOPTION_GUIDE.md and verify_config.sample.yaml, including a preflight checklist within. \n\nOnce those files are written, I’ll check the storage list to confirm their existence.\
  \ After that, I’ll create a session log in private memory and update the meta prompt to reflect the current phase of adoption support, including monitoring replies and scheduling the v2.1 patch if needed. Let's keep things concise!"
