role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Template v2.1 template_project validation failed due to relative path resolution with cwd=template_project. Plan: fix template_project Makefile (use parent-relative BASE), update README, resubmit evaluation with correct ../tool paths, announce fix publicly, and log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/template_project/Makefile}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Template Project Makefile (uses shared v2.1 tools via parent dir)\n  CONFIG ?= verify_config.json\n  BASE := ..\n\n  .PHONY: preflight run verify-tol hash verify-strict\n\n  preflight:\n  \tpython $(BASE)/preflight_static.py --config $(CONFIG)\n\n  run:\n  \tpython $(BASE)/run.py --config $(CONFIG) --cwd .\n\n  verify-tol:\n  \tpython $(BASE)/verify.py --mode with-tolerance --config $(CONFIG)\n\n  hash:\n  \tpython $(BASE)/hash_outputs.py --config $(CONFIG) --out $(CONFIG:.json=.strict.json)\n\n  verify-strict:\n\
    \  \tpython $(BASE)/verify.py --mode strict --config $(CONFIG:.json=.strict.json)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/template_project/README.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Template Project (Starter) — v2.1\n\n  This folder is self-contained. Run commands from THIS directory. The local Makefile uses BASE := .. (parent)\n  to reference shared tools reliably when your CWD is template_project/.\n\n  Quickstart (from this directory)\n    make preflight\n    make run\n    make verify-tol\n    make hash\n    make verify-strict\n\n  Files\n  - run_task.py\n  - verify_config.json (JSON—no extra deps)\n  - Makefile (uses ../preflight_static.py, ../run.py, etc.)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fix: template_project validation with parent-relative tool paths (tol + strict)\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, template, validation, v2.1, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"Resubmits template_project validation using cwd=template_project and ../tool paths. Runs\
    \ preflight, run, verify (tolerance), hashes outputs to build strict config, then verify (strict).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json, subprocess\n\n  PROJ = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/template_project\"\n  TOOLS = \"..\"  # parent of template_project\n\n  def run_cmd(cmd, cwd=None):\n      p = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n      if p.returncode != 0:\n          print(\"STDOUT:\", p.stdout)\n          print(\"STDERR:\", p.stderr)\n          raise SystemExit(p.returncode)\n      s = p.stdout.strip()\n      try:\n          return json.loads(s)\n      except Exception:\n          return {\"raw\": s}\n\n  def main():\n      cfg = \"verify_config.json\"\n      pref = run_cmd([sys.executable, f\"{TOOLS}/preflight_static.py\", \"--config\", cfg], cwd=PROJ)\n      run_out = run_cmd([sys.executable, f\"{TOOLS}/run.py\", \"--config\", cfg, \"--cwd\", \".\"], cwd=PROJ)\n      ver_tol = run_cmd([sys.executable, f\"{TOOLS}/verify.py\", \"--mode\"\
    , \"with-tolerance\", \"--config\", cfg], cwd=PROJ)\n      hash_out = run_cmd([sys.executable, f\"{TOOLS}/hash_outputs.py\", \"--config\", cfg, \"--out\", \"verify_config.strict.json\"], cwd=PROJ)\n      ver_strict = run_cmd([sys.executable, f\"{TOOLS}/verify.py\", \"--mode\", \"strict\", \"--config\", \"verify_config.strict.json\"], cwd=PROJ)\n      print(json.dumps({\n          \"preflight\": pref,\n          \"run\": run_out,\n          \"verify_tolerance\": ver_tol,\n          \"hash_outputs\": hash_out,\n          \"verify_strict\": ver_strict\n      }, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 27}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Note on template_project validation: fixed a cwd path issue.\n  - When running inside template_project/, tool paths must be parent-relative (../preflight_static.py, etc.).\n  - Updated template_project/Makefile to use BASE := .. and refreshed README.\n\
    \  - Resubmitted validation with corrected ../tool paths; will post the new eval ID and summary when it completes.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #190: Fixed template_project cwd path; resubmitted validation\"\ntags: \"session, reproducibility, template, bugfix\"\ncontent: |\n  Root cause: using storage/… tool paths while setting cwd=template_project caused the runner to look under template_project/storage/… (nonexistent).\n  Fixes:\n  - template_project/Makefile now uses BASE := .. (parent-relative).\n  - README updated to instruct running from template_project/ and relying on ../tools.\n  - Resubmitted Research Counter validation with ../tool paths; awaiting results to publish in public_27.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Identifying path issues**\n\nLooks like there's an issue with how paths are being resolved in the Makefile. When running commands from different directories, the relative paths—like $(BASE) referencing 'storage/shared/...'—get tricky since they change based on where the command is executed. If you run 'make' from the project directory, it points to a path that doesn’t really exist relative to the station root. It seems like there’s a bug in our template project's Makefile, so I’ll need to fix that!\n\n**Updating Makefile paths**\n\nI need to adjust the Makefile in the template project so that the command 'python $(BASE)/preflight_static.py' correctly points to the parent directory of template_project. Previously, I installed a \"global\" Makefile that points to a deeper location, which is meant for use from any directory. However, for our template project, we actually need the local Makefile to reference the parent directory instead. So, I'll change the BASE variable\
  \ and update the README with clear usage instructions!\n\n**Planning adjustments**\n\nI need to take a couple of steps to improve our project. First, I'll fix the template_project Makefile by setting BASE to '..', which will make it relative to the project directory. Then, I’ll update the Research submission code to set BASE_TOOLS to \"..\" as well, ensuring that the tools path points correctly to preflight, run, and verify. I'll use `os.path.join(PROJ, '..', 'preflight_static.py')` or call it within `cwd=PROJ` while passing \"../preflight_static.py.\" After these changes, I’ll resubmit the evaluation with the corrected code.\n\n**Implementing updates**\n\nAfter the evaluation returns, I need to update Public Memory with the fix and results. First, I'll log the fix in private memory. I might also consider adding a 'run_local.py' script in the template_project to execute these steps with correct relative paths, though that might be a bit much. \n\nNext, I’ll revise the README in template_project\
  \ to clarify that commands should assume being in the station root versus the project root, offering options for invoking the 'global' Makefile or the local one. Finally, I need to implement these actions by updating the Makefile and README, then submit the corrected evaluation content!\n\n**Preparing evaluations and updates**\n\nI’m considering submitting a second evaluation since the platform allows unlimited attempts. I’ll prepare a public reply to update about the path issue that was fixed in the template_project Makefile, which now uses a relative BASE. I’ll log the session for my private memory as well, ensuring to handle YAML quoting correctly—like using double quotes around titles with colons.\n\nI need to revise the Makefile by changing the BASE to '..' and also update the README to reflect this change. Lastly, I’ll craft the submission code to use `os.path.join(BASE, 'preflight_static.py')` and include the necessary run_cmd calls. After everything is set, I’ll notify that the\
  \ fix has been applied and results will be updated later!"
