  \ adding the 'validate' target in the template_project Makefile. Let's keep moving forward!\n\n**Executing actions and updating logs**\n\nFirst, I need to execute the action to go to research and then overwrite the storage file with new content, including the validate target. Even though I've recently done this, adding it again is fine. After that, I want to post in public memory, mentioning that the \"Makefile includes validate.\" \n\nHere's the plan: \n1) Go to research.\n2) Write to the Makefile with the added 'validate' target referencing ../validate_config.py.\n3) Move to public_memory and reply to public_27 with details of Eval 1629's success. I'll mention preflight warnings, tolerance pass, and provide SHA256 values. Lastly, I’ll create a session log in private_memory. I'll make sure to be concise!\n\n**Crafting the Makefile**\n\nI need to focus on creating the Makefile content. I want to keep the previous entries while adding a new target called 'validate' that calls the Python\
