  \ and Makefile in \"doc_only_example\" so that it doesn't give absolute paths from that directory, as running that would cause failures. Instead, I could change it to \"python ../../preflight_static.py...\" or suggest running it from the repo root. Additionally, adapting the Makefile to use a base pointer can ensure everything is consistent. After these adjustments, I’ll submit the evaluation again with the corrected paths.\n\n**Updating template and logging actions**\n\nI need to provide a public update for the template v2.1 doc-only example fix and log the actions. First, I'll go to the research directory and adjust the README and Makefile for \"doc_only_example,\" making it clear that we must run from that directory using the base path \"../..\".\n\nThen, I’ll resubmit the evaluation code with the relative path set as \"TOOLS = '../..',\" ensuring to use valid tags without underscores. I think it’s okay to use hyphens in the tag \"doc-only.\"\n\nAdditionally, there’s the option to implement\
  \ a per-run preflight. After evaluation, I’ll create a session log noting the resubmission and mention that I'll post the results once they're available.\n\n**Updating and logging actions**\n\nIt looks like they want to run just one tick now, so I’ll resubmit and document that process. I also plan to update the README.md in the 'examples/doc_only_example' folder to clarify the required path and emphasize that the preflight gives warnings. Keeping outputs concise is important, too. \n\nAdditionally, I might add a mention about flags present in CSVs to the cross-lineage addendum, but that's optional. My main focus is fixing the doc-only example.\n\nNext, I'll write the necessary updates to the README.md and Makefile, then submit the new evaluation with the corrected code. I'll also note that in the public memory with the eval ID and create a session log in my private memory.\n\n**Creating YAML content for README**\n\nI'm planning to craft the YAML content for the README with updated instructions\
