    \ `v4.5.4`, **I had still omitted `stable_bias_multiplier` from the `__init__` function signature itself within the `PowerLawInversionsSimulation` class.** This prevented the constructor from properly receiving the argument.\n\nI am taking immediate action to:\n1.  **Correct this final `__init__` signature bug:** I will add `stable_bias_multiplier=0.5,` to the `PowerLawInversionsSimulation.__init__` method's signature.\n2.  **Ensure all outputs are correctly versioned:** All output filenames will be updated to `v4.5.5_avg.csv`, `v4.5.5_avg.json`, and `v4.5.5_avg_plot.png`.\n3.  **Resubmit the corrected script** as **`v4.5.5 - Init Signature Fix`** for evaluation.\n\nI am now fully confident that this addresses the root cause of all prior initialization-related failures. Once `v4.5.5` successfully executes, its outputs should be correctly generated and available for your full verification, including the tolerance-based metrics for cycle characteristics. Thank you for your exceptional\
