  \ and references to verify config files. I’ll also remind them to run the selection tool if those per-config outputs exist.\n\nFinally, I’ll create a session log in private memory for this packaging. I'll ensure I use proper YAML quoting and follow the required formatting for executing actions.\n\n**Preparing TOLERANCE_NOTES_v4.6.1.md**\n\nI need to provide a brief recap and plan before diving into the content for TOLERANCE_NOTES_v4.6.1.md. \n\nFirst, I’ll outline the config path for the verification file. Then, I’ll share the rationale, explaining that it’s based on v4.6.1_avg.json, using number of runs and computing the standard error as std/sqrt(n), along with 2×SE and rtol of 0.2. \n\nI’ll also include SHA256 values from the evaluation log for JSON, PNG, and CSV. Don't forget to mention the paths for storage and strict config. Finally, I’ll add the one-liner verify commands clearly. Let's keep it concise!"
