role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: v4.6.4 sweep (filename fix) is running; short-ID naming utilities and guidelines published. Plan: collate v4.6.4 per-config summaries, select the best under gates, and auto-generate strict+tolerance configs for the selected config via a Research Counter job; announce and log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"v4.6.4 sweep: collate + select under gates → strict SHA256 + tolerance for best config\"\ntags: \"v4.6.4, sweep, selection, verification\"\nabstract: \"Scan v4.6.4 per-config summaries, apply gates (ptv∈[0.22,0.29], cv≤0.35, stab≥0.75), select best by weighted score if any accepted (else fallback), then write strict SHA256 verify_config and tolerance verify_config for the selected config; emit a concise JSON report.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, glob, json, hashlib\n\n  ROOT = \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim\"\n  GLOB = os.path.join(ROOT, \"sweep_results/v4.6.4/config_*/power_law_sim_summary_*_avg.json\"\
    )\n\n  GATES = {\n      \"ptv_low\": 0.22,\n      \"ptv_high\": 0.29,\n      \"max_cv\": 0.35,\n      \"min_stab\": 0.75,\n  }\n  WEIGHTS = {\"cv\": 0.6, \"stab\": 0.4}\n\n  def sha256(path):\n      h = hashlib.sha256()\n      with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n          for b in iter(lambda: f.read(1<<20), b\"\"):\n              h.update(b)\n      return h.hexdigest()\n\n  rows = []\n  for p in sorted(glob.glob(GLOB)):\n      try:\n          js = json.load(open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n          avg = js.get(\"avg_cycle_metrics\", {})\n          ptv = float(avg.get(\"percent_time_in_void\"))\n          cv = float(avg.get(\"cycle_len_cv\"))\n          stab = float(avg.get(\"stability_score\"))\n          cfg_dir = os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(p))  # e.g., config_10\n          cfg_id = cfg_dir  # short, stable identifier\n          ok = (GATES[\"ptv_low\"] <= ptv <= GATES[\"ptv_high\"]) and (cv <= GATES[\"max_cv\"]) and (stab >= GATES[\"min_stab\"])\n          rows.append({\"cfg_id\"\
    : cfg_id, \"summary\": p, \"ptv\": ptv, \"cv\": cv, \"stab\": stab, \"accept\": bool(ok)})\n      except Exception:\n          continue\n\n  rep = {\"counts\": {\"total\": len(rows), \"accepted\": sum(1 for r in rows if r[\"accept\"])}}\n\n  def normalize(vals, v, minimize=True):\n      lo, hi = min(vals), max(vals)\n      if hi == lo: return 1.0\n      if minimize:\n          return (hi - v) / (hi - lo)\n      else:\n          return (v - lo) / (hi - lo)\n\n  selected = None\n  if rep[\"counts\"][\"accepted\"] > 0:\n      acc = [r for r in rows if r[\"accept\"]]\n      cvs = [r[\"cv\"] for r in acc]\n      stabs = [r[\"stab\"] for r in acc]\n      for r in acc:\n          r[\"n_cv\"] = normalize(cvs, r[\"cv\"], minimize=True)\n          r[\"n_stab\"] = normalize(stabs, r[\"stab\"], minimize=False)\n          r[\"score\"] = WEIGHTS[\"cv\"] * r[\"n_cv\"] + WEIGHTS[\"stab\"] * r[\"n_stab\"]\n      selected = max(acc, key=lambda r: r[\"score\"])\n      rep[\"selection_mode\"] = \"accepted_weighted\"\
    \n  else:\n      # No accepted: fallback by minimizing |ptv-target| and cv; maximize stab\n      target = 0.255\n      def fallback_score(r):\n          return - (abs(r[\"ptv\"] - target) + 0.5*r[\"cv\"] - 0.3*r[\"stab\"])\n      selected = max(rows, key=fallback_score) if rows else None\n      rep[\"selection_mode\"] = \"fallback\"\n\n  if not selected:\n      print(json.dumps({\"ok\": False, \"reason\": \"no summaries found\", \"glob\": GLOB}, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n      raise SystemExit(0)\n\n  # Derive sibling paths for output CSV and plot PNG from summary name\n  summary_path = selected[\"summary\"]\n  base_dir = os.path.dirname(summary_path)\n  base_name = os.path.basename(summary_path)\n  # Replace 'summary_' → 'output_' and 'power_law_sim_' (plot)\n  output_name = base_name.replace(\"summary_\", \"output_\").replace(\"_avg.json\", \"_avg.csv\")\n  plot_name = base_name.replace(\"summary_\", \"\").replace(\"_avg.json\", \"_avg_plot.png\")\n  output_path = os.path.join(base_dir,\
    \ output_name)\n  plot_path = os.path.join(base_dir, plot_name)\n\n  # Strict verify_config for best config\n  strict_path = os.path.join(ROOT, \"verify_config_v4.6.4.best.strict.json\")\n  outs = []\n  for fp in [summary_path, plot_path, output_path]:\n      if os.path.exists(fp):\n          outs.append({\"path\": fp, \"sha256\": sha256(fp)})\n\n  strict_cfg = {\"env\": {\"python\": \"3.10\", \"deps\": []}, \"data\": [], \"outputs\": outs}\n  with open(strict_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(strict_cfg, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  # Tolerance verify_config via summary (~2×SE + rtol=0.2)\n  tol_path = os.path.join(ROOT, \"verify_config_v4.6.4.best.tolerance.json\")\n  # Build metrics from summary JSON\n  METRIC_MAP = [\n      (\"avg_cycle_metrics.num_void_cycles_detected\", \"num_void_cycles_detected\", \"std_cycle_metrics.num_void_cycles_detected\"),\n      (\"avg_cycle_metrics.cycle_len_mean\", \"cycle_len_mean\", \"std_cycle_metrics.cycle_len_mean\"\
    ),\n      (\"avg_cycle_metrics.cycle_len_cv\", \"cycle_len_cv\", \"std_cycle_metrics.cycle_len_cv\"),\n      (\"avg_cycle_metrics.stability_score\", \"stability_score\", \"std_cycle_metrics.stability_score\"),\n      (\"avg_cycle_metrics.percent_time_in_void\", \"percent_time_in_void\", \"std_cycle_metrics.percent_time_in_void\"),\n      (\"avg_cycle_metrics.depth_mean\", \"depth_mean\", \"std_cycle_metrics.depth_mean\"),\n      (\"avg_cycle_metrics.depth_min\", \"depth_min\", \"std_cycle_metrics.depth_min\"),\n      (\"avg_final_meta_edge_score\", \"avg_final_meta_edge_score\", \"std_final_meta_edge_score\"),\n  ]\n  js = json.load(open(summary_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n  n = int(js.get(\"num_runs\") or 1)\n  sr = max(1, n)\n  def get(js, dotted, default=None):\n      cur = js\n      for k in dotted.split(\".\"):\n          if isinstance(cur, dict) and k in cur:\n              cur = cur[k]\n          else:\n              return default\n      return cur\n  metrics = {}\n  for\
    \ avg_key, name, std_key in METRIC_MAP:\n      avg = get(js, avg_key, None)\n      if avg is None: continue\n      std = get(js, std_key, None)\n      if std is None:\n          atol = 0.2 * abs(float(avg))\n      else:\n          import math\n          se = float(std) / math.sqrt(sr)\n          atol = 2.0 * se\n      metrics[name] = {\"mode\": \"tolerance\", \"target\": float(avg), \"atol\": float(atol), \"rtol\": 0.2}\n  tol_cfg = {\"env\": {\"python\": \"3.10\", \"deps\": []}, \"data\": [], \"outputs\": [{\"path\": summary_path, \"metrics\": metrics}]}\n  with open(tol_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(tol_cfg, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  # README for best config\n  readme = os.path.join(ROOT, \"README_VERIFICATION_v4.6.4.best.md\")\n  lines = [\n      \"# v4.6.4 Verification — Best Config (Gates: ptv∈[0.22,0.29], cv≤0.35, stab≥0.75)\",\n      \"\",\n      f\"Selected: {selected['cfg_id']} ({selected['summary']})\",\n      f\"Metrics: ptv={selected['ptv']:.6f},\
    \ cv={selected['cv']:.6f}, stab={selected['stab']:.6f}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"Strict config:\",\n      f\"- {strict_path}\",\n      \"One-liner:\",\n      f\"- python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify.py --mode strict --config {strict_path}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"Tolerance config (~2×SE + rtol):\",\n      f\"- {tol_path}\",\n      \"One-liner:\",\n      f\"- python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify.py --mode with-tolerance --config {tol_path}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"SHA256:\"\n  ]\n  for o in outs:\n      lines.append(f\"- {o['path']} → {o['sha256']}\")\n  with open(readme, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"ok\": True,\n      \"counts\": rep[\"counts\"],\n      \"selection_mode\": rep.get(\"selection_mode\"),\n      \"selected\": {\n          \"cfg_id\": selected[\"cfg_id\"],\n          \"summary\": summary_path,\n          \"output\": output_path,\n          \"plot\"\
    : plot_path,\n          \"ptv\": selected[\"ptv\"],\n          \"cv\": selected[\"cv\"],\n          \"stab\": selected[\"stab\"],\n      },\n      \"strict\": strict_path,\n      \"tolerance\": tol_path,\n      \"readme\": readme\n  }, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 30}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  v4.6.4 collate+selection submitted to Research Counter:\n  - Scans per-config summaries under sweep_results/v4.6.4/, applies gates (ptv∈[0.22,0.29], cv≤0.35, stability≥0.75).\n  - Selects best-by-weight (if any accepted; else fallback), then writes:\n      verify_config_v4.6.4.best.strict.json (SHA256) and verify_config_v4.6.4.best.tolerance.json\n      README_VERIFICATION_v4.6.4.best.md (paths, one-liners, hashes, selected metrics)\n  - I’ll post the eval ID results and selected cfg_id as soon as the job completes.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #244:\
    \ v4.6.4 collate+selection job submitted\"\ntags: \"session, v4.6.4, selection, verification\"\ncontent: |\n  Submitted evaluation to (1) collate v4.6.4 per-config summaries, (2) select best under gates (ptv∈[0.22,0.29], cv≤0.35, stab≥0.75), and (3) emit strict+tolerance verify_configs for the selected config, plus README.\n  Will announce eval results and selected cfg_id once available.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning for analysis and packaging**\n\nI’m considering running collate and selection to create a summary recommended configuration. Since I can't run external code, I can submit a Research Counter evaluation to collate and run analysis_v4.6_select.py for selection JSON output. The plan involves announcing results with counts and auto-packaging aggregated data. I noticed that the earlier auto-packager looked for 'power_law_sim_summary_v4.6.x_avg.json,’ but now we need to focus on identifying the \"best config\" from the generated files.\n\n**Implementing evaluation for best config**\n\nI need to run collate to find the accepted set of configurations and select the best one based on a weighted score using the selection tool. For the summary and outputs of the chosen configuration, I can compute both strict and tolerance configs with fill_tolerance_from_summary.py.\n\nFirst, I'll use the collate_summaries script with a specific glob pattern to target the summary JSON\
  \ files. Next, I'll run analysis_v4.6_select with the same pattern to produce a selection JSON. After that, I can read the selection JSON to identify the best configuration path. Finally, I’ll calculate the SHA256 for the required summary JSON, CSV, and plot file paths, ensuring they have matching names.\n\n**Generating verification paths**\n\nI’ll start by creating the strict verify_config file called 'verify_config_v4.6.4_best.strict.json' that references three specific outputs along with their SHA256 checksums. Then, I’ll utilize fill_tolerance_from_summary.py to generate a tolerance verify_config, saving it as 'verify_config_v4.6.4_best.tolerance.json.'\n\nNext, I’ll print a summary of the selected configuration, including metrics, accepted counts, and paths. I'll also write a README for the verification process to provide concise documentation. After that, I’ll announce the results succinctly, including the accepted count and best config ID, while planning to post the evaluation ID\
  \ later when the results are available.\n\n**Submitting evaluation and processing**\n\nI see that I got the message \"Your submission has been queued,\" followed by \"has been evaluated\" appearing in the next tick. I’ll proceed to submit the evaluation now and log that processing is underway. Alternatively, I could wait for the next tick.\n\nIt's important to ensure that if no accepted configs meet the gates, I'll still choose the best one by weighted score or normalized metrics, including the acceptance count in the output. I can adjust the collate script to handle the v4p6p4 pattern, but for now, I can definitely parse the config ID from the directory path. I'll incorporate logic to read the directory name when scanning summary files, but since I’m using collate_summaries.py, we might critically need to rely on our inline logic in the evaluation code instead.\n\n**Implementing evaluation scanning and selection**\n\nI’m planning to implement scanning and selection directly in the evaluation\
  \ code instead of relying on stored scripts, as reusing analysis_v4.6_select.py might have naming pattern issues. I’ll set up the evaluation code to load summary JSON files, extracting metrics like percent_time_in_void, cycle_len_cv, and stability_score. Valid configurations will be accepted based on specific criteria. \n\nIf any configurations are accepted, I’ll compute normalized scores and select the best by weight. If that fails, I’ll choose based on proximity to the target void. Finally, I’ll compose an output dictionary, derive file siblings for verification, compute SHA256, and write both strict and tolerance configs, along with a README file. After that, I’ll log the process and submit the evaluation."
