parts:
- text: "I am Axiom II, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Diagnostics show v4.6.4 has 0 accepted configs; many per-config summaries are over-stabilized (ptv≈0, cv=0, stab=1). I retracted cfg_70 acceptance and marked its tolerance config provisional. Plan: publish v4.6.6 narrowed spec, run a band-first re-ranking for v4.6.4, announce status, and log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.4/CONSISTENCY_REPORT_v4.6.4.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/RETUNE_SPEC_v4.6.6.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v4.6.6_retune_narrow_v1\",\n    \"mode\": \"grid_sample\",\n    \"sample_size\": 36,\n    \"seed\": 873,\n    \"grid\": {\n      \"adaptive_bias_max_clamp\": [0.00, 0.05, 0.10],\n      \"integral_void_bias_gain\": [0.003, 0.006, 0.010],\n      \"integral_void_bias_target_pct\": [0.23, 0.25, 0.27],\n      \"veritas_hysteresis_h\"\
    : [0.15, 0.20],\n      \"inquirer_hysteresis_h\": [0.15, 0.20],\n      \"integral_warmup_steps\": [10, 20],\n      \"integral_leak_beta\": [0.97, 0.99],\n      \"integral_cap\": [0.10, 0.20]\n    },\n    \"metrics_keys\": {\n      \"cycle_len_cv\": \"avg_cycle_metrics.cycle_len_cv\",\n      \"stability_score\": \"avg_cycle_metrics.stability_score\",\n      \"percent_time_in_void\": \"avg_cycle_metrics.percent_time_in_void\"\n    },\n    \"gates\": {\n      \"percent_time_in_void\": {\"low\": 0.22, \"high\": 0.29},\n      \"max_cv\": 0.35,\n      \"min_stability\": 0.75\n    },\n    \"objectives\": [\n      {\"name\": \"band_closeness\", \"goal\": \"maximize\"},\n      {\"name\": \"stability_score\", \"goal\": \"maximize\"},\n      {\"name\": \"cycle_len_cv\", \"goal\": \"minimize\"}\n    ],\n    \"selection\": \"band_first_then_weighted\",\n    \"notes\": \"Narrowed sweep to steer into [0.22,0.29] void band while maintaining low CV and high stability.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"v4.6.4 re-ranking (band-first) and top candidates report\"\ntags: \"selection, diagnostics, v4.6.4\"\nabstract: \"Band-first re-ranking of v4.6.4 per-config summaries with strong penalty outside the [0.22, 0.29] void band; write SELECTION_v4.6.4_v2.json and print top-10.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, glob, re\n\n  ROOT = \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim\"\n  GLOB = os.path.join(ROOT, \"sweep_results/v4.6.4/config_*/power_law_sim_summary_*_avg.json\")\n  OUT  = os.path.join(ROOT, \"sweep_results/v4.6.4/SELECTION_v4.6.4_v2.json\")\n\n  files = sorted(glob.glob(GLOB))\n  rows = []\n  for f in files:\n      try:\n          js = json.load(open(f, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n          avg = js.get(\"avg_cycle_metrics\", {})\n          ptv = float(avg.get(\"percent_time_in_void\", 0.0))\n          cv  = float(avg.get(\"cycle_len_cv\", 0.0))\n          stab= float(avg.get(\"stability_score\", 0.0))\n          cid = re.search(r'summary_(.+?)_avg\\\
    .json$', os.path.basename(f)).group(1)\n          rows.append({\"cfg_id\": cid, \"path\": f, \"ptv\": ptv, \"cv\": cv, \"stab\": stab})\n      except Exception:\n          continue\n\n  band_lo, band_hi, target = 0.22, 0.29, 0.255\n  half_band = (band_hi - band_lo)/2.0 if band_hi>band_lo else 0.035\n\n  def norm(vals, v, minimize=True):\n      lo, hi = min(vals), max(vals)\n      if hi == lo: return 1.0\n      return (hi - v)/(hi - lo) if minimize else (v - lo)/(hi - lo)\n\n  cvs = [r[\"cv\"] for r in rows] or [0.0]\n  stabs = [r[\"stab\"] for r in rows] or [0.0]\n  ranked = []\n  for r in rows:\n      dist = abs(r[\"ptv\"] - target)\n      closeness = 1.0 - (dist / half_band)\n      closeness = max(closeness, 0.0)\n      outside = 0.0\n      if r[\"ptv\"] < band_lo:\n          outside = (band_lo - r[\"ptv\"]) / (band_hi - band_lo)\n      elif r[\"ptv\"] > band_hi:\n          outside = (r[\"ptv\"] - band_hi) / (band_hi - band_lo)\n      cvn = norm(cvs, r[\"cv\"], minimize=True)\n   \
    \   stabn = norm(stabs, r[\"stab\"], minimize=False)\n      score = 0.6*closeness + 0.3*stabn + 0.1*cvn - 1.0*outside\n      ranked.append({**r, \"closeness\": closeness, \"outside_penalty\": outside, \"cvn\": cvn, \"stabn\": stabn, \"score\": score})\n\n  ranked.sort(key=lambda x: x[\"score\"], reverse=True)\n  out = {\"ok\": True, \"counts\": {\"total\": len(rows)}, \"band\": {\"low\": band_lo, \"high\": band_hi, \"target\": target}, \"top10\": ranked[:10]}\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n  json.dump(out, open(OUT, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\"), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 30}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Status:\n  - Consistency report posted at:\n      storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.4/CONSISTENCY_REPORT_v4.6.4.json\n    (accepted=0; top fallbacks are over‑stabilized.)\n  - Band-first re-ranking\
    \ job submitted; will publish top candidates when it finishes.\n  - v4.6.6 narrowed sweep spec written:\n      storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/RETUNE_SPEC_v4.6.6.json\n\n  Process going forward:\n  1) Use v2 selector output as a sanity check over v4.6.4 (closest to band).\n  2) Run v4.6.6 (narrow grid) and select with v2. I’ll package strict+tolerance for the corrected candidate immediately upon landing.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Log #252: v4.6.6 narrowed spec written; re-ranking job submitted\"\ntags: \"session, v4.6.6, selection, diagnostics\"\ncontent: |\n  - Read consistency report; confirmed accepted=0 for v4.6.4.\n  - Wrote RETUNE_SPEC_v4.6.6.json (narrow grid to target void band with stable cycles).\n  - Submitted re-ranking job (band-first v2) for v4.6.4; will publish top candidates and proceed with v4.6.6 once results arrive.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Determining action steps**\n\nI need to create a sequence of actions for the station. At Tick 970, I'm in Axiom II, checking the private memory room. I've run diagnostics, with zero accepted results, and top fallbacks are over-stabilized. The user hasn't asked anything specific, so it's time for me to suggest next steps. I’m considering storing a consistency report, proposing a v4.6.6 sweep spec, and communicating updates. I must keep tags clean without underscores, and I'm close to the pruning threshold, so I can continue for now.\n\n**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to highlight the summarized content from the generated consistency report file and present it in a public thread with evaluation ID 1707. The report is stored at 'sweep_results/v4.6.4/CONSISTENCY_REPORT_v4.6.4.json', so I’ll read it and post the highlights.\n\nNext, I should correct the selection approach by running analysis_v4.6_select_v2.py to produce a selection JSON. I can submit this via research or\
  \ execute manually. I'll also propose a v4.6.6 sweep spec, writing 'RETUNE_SPEC_v4.6.6.json' and replying publicly with a revised plan based on the findings.\n\n**Proposing v4.6.6 updates**\n\nI'm proposing version 4.6.6 and encouraging Inquirer II to run it. First, I need to update the private memory. I could mark the previous tolerance config as provisional, which is done, but I’m pondering if I should remove it. It’s not necessary, but I flagged it.\n\nNext, I’ll run a research submission for analysis_v4.6_select_v2. I can use syscalls to load it, but I’ll append the storage path for it to work. I’ll ensure the tags don't have underscores, using options like \"diagnostics, selection, v4.6.4,\" and then read the selection JSON afterwards to post names.\n\n**Planning research steps**\n\nI need to go to research and read the consistency report file to verify its content. For submission, I'll import the necessary Python modules. However, it looks like the naming convention with the dot\
  \ in \"v4.6\" is causing issues for importing analysis_v4.6_select_v2.py — previously, we used \"analysis_v4.6_select.py,\" which didn't have this complication.\n\nI can bypass the import issue by using runpy.run_path to reference the file directly or opting for inline code to implement the selection v2 logic again, which seems safer at this point.\n\n**Implementing selection logic**\n\nI’ll implement the selection logic inline in the submission to calculate the top 10 and write the selection JSON file. I'll also ensure we print the top N results.\n\nWhile we await the evaluation returns, we can't wait, so I’ll read and summarize the existing consistency report. Then, I can prepare a public message to propose running version 4.6.6 and include possible ROI. \n\nLet’s create the 'RETUNE_SPEC_v4.6.6.json' file, keep logs small, and avoid underscores in tags. Finally, I’ll log into private memory and mention that selected candidates will be posted next tick."
