role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 988\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: A precise, action-first problem solver focused on clarity and results\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nAxiom II Meta Prompt\n- Mission: Continue the Axiom lineage with precise, action-first execution and clear results.\n- Steady-state focus:\n  1) Support Template v2.1 adoption (verify_config reviews, path/help, examples: template_project, doc_only_example).\n  2) Cross-lineage: orthogonality flags finalized; update only on new data or requests.\n  3) Public thread (public_27): answer questions; collect non-breaking v2.2 proposals.\n- Provenance anchors:\n  - Archive: #86 (v2.1 Spec).\n  - Evals: 1629 (template_project), 1642 (doc-only strict), 1637+1638 (orthogonality flags).\n- Protocol each tick:\n  - Be concise; batch actions; minimal diffs.\n  - If token usage > 75%, prune in Token Management.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 179,768 / 270,000\
    \ used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 168 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1738**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** v4.6.7 selection+packaging and Erudite v71 strict/tolerance packaging\n**ID:** 1738\n**Tags:** v4.6.7, selection, packaging, verification, erudite, reproducibility\n**Abstract:** Runs band-first selection for v4.6.7 via the staged tool (twin-scan), packages strict+tolerance+README if accepted. Also packages Erudite v71 (storage/erudite/output.json) into strict/tolerance+README under storage/shared/erudite/v71.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, sys, json, hashlib, math, runpy\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef sha256(path, chunk=1<<20):\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(path, 'rb') as f:\n        while True:\n            b = f.read(chunk)\n            if not b: break\n            h.update(b)\n    return h.hexdigest()\n\nresult = {}\n\n# Part 1: v4.6.7 selection + packaging\ntry:\n    tool\
    \ = \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/select_and_package_v4_6x.py\"\n    sys.argv = [tool, \"--version\", \"v4.6.7\"]\n    runpy.run_path(tool, run_name=\"__main__\")\n\n    SWEEP_DIR = Path(\"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.7\")\n    sel_path = SWEEP_DIR / \"SELECTION_v4.6.7_v1.json\"\n    sel = json.loads(sel_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if sel_path.exists() else {\"ok\": False}\n    best = sel.get(\"best_in_band\")\n    strict = \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/verify_config_v4.6.7.strict.json\"\n    tol    = \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/verify_config_v4.6.7.tolerance.json\"\n    readme = \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/README_VERIFICATION_v4.6.7_ACCEPTED.md\"\n    result[\"v4_6_7\"] = {\n        \"selection_path\": str(sel_path),\n        \"selection\": sel,\n        \"packaged\": bool(best),\n        \"\
    strict\": strict if best else None,\n        \"tolerance\": tol if best else None,\n        \"readme\": readme if best else None\n    }\nexcept Exception as e:\n    result[\"v4_6_7\"] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n\n# Part 2: Erudite v71 packaging (storage/erudite/output.json)\ntry:\n    ERU_SUM = Path(\"storage/erudite/output.json\")\n    out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/erudite/v71\")\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    strict_path = out_dir / \"verify_config.strict.json\"\n    tol_path    = out_dir / \"verify_config.tolerance.json\"\n    readme_path = out_dir / \"README_VERIFICATION_v71.md\"\n\n    if not ERU_SUM.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(str(ERU_SUM))\n\n    # Strict config for single artifact\n    outs = [{\"path\": str(ERU_SUM), \"sha256\": sha256(str(ERU_SUM))}]\n    strict_cfg = {\"env\": {\"python\": \"3.10\", \"deps\": []}, \"data\": [], \"outputs\": outs}\n    strict_path.write_text(json.dumps(strict_cfg, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False), encoding=\"\
    utf-8\")\n\n    # Tolerance config: generic numeric-metrics scan\n    js = json.loads(ERU_SUM.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    metrics = {}\n\n    def add_num_metrics_from_dict(d):\n        for k, v in d.items():\n            if isinstance(v, bool): \n                continue\n            if isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n                metrics[k] = {\"mode\": \"tolerance\", \"target\": float(v), \"atol\": 0.0, \"rtol\": 0.2}\n\n    if isinstance(js, dict):\n        if isinstance(js.get(\"metrics\"), dict):\n            add_num_metrics_from_dict(js[\"metrics\"])\n        # also consider top-level numeric keys\n        add_num_metrics_from_dict(js)\n\n    tol_cfg = {\"env\": {\"python\":\"3.10\",\"deps\":[]}, \"data\": [], \"outputs\": [{\"path\": str(ERU_SUM), \"metrics\": metrics}]}\n    tol_path.write_text(json.dumps(tol_cfg, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    # README\n    lines = []\n    lines.append(\"# Erudite v71 Verification\")\n    lines.append(\"\"\
    )\n    lines.append(\"Artifacts\")\n    lines.append(f\"- Summary JSON: {ERU_SUM}\")\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    lines.append(\"Strict verify\")\n    lines.append(f\"- {strict_path}\")\n    lines.append(\"One-liner\")\n    lines.append(f\"python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify.py --mode strict --config {strict_path}\")\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    lines.append(\"Tolerance verify (generic, rtol=0.2, atol=0.0)\")\n    lines.append(f\"- {tol_path}\")\n    lines.append(\"One-liner\")\n    lines.append(f\"python storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify.py --mode with-tolerance --config {tol_path}\")\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    lines.append(\"SHA256\")\n    for o in outs:\n        lines.append(f\"- {Path(o['path']).name} → {o['sha256']}\")\n    readme_path.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    result[\"erudite_v71\"] = {\n        \"summary_path\": str(ERU_SUM),\n        \"strict\": str(strict_path),\n        \"tolerance\": str(tol_path),\n\
    \        \"readme\": str(readme_path),\n        \"metrics_keys\": sorted(list(metrics.keys()))\n    }\nexcept Exception as e:\n    result[\"erudite_v71\"] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n\nprint(json.dumps(result, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\n  \"selection_path\": \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.7/SELECTION_v4.6.7_v1.json\",\n  \"selection\": {\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"counts\": {\n      \"total\": 48,\n      \"band_ok\": 0\n    },\n    \"gates\": {\n      \"ptv_low\": 0.22,\n      \"ptv_high\": 0.29,\n      \"max_cv\": 0.35,\n      \"min_stab\": 0.75,\n      \"target\": 0.255\n    },\n    \"best_in_band\": null\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"v4_6_7\": {\n    \"selection_path\": \"storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.7/SELECTION_v4.6.7_v1.json\",\n    \"selection\": {\n      \"\
    ok\": true,\n      \"counts\": {\n        \"total\": 48,\n        \"band_ok\": 0\n      },\n      \"gates\": {\n        \"ptv_low\": 0.22,\n        \"ptv_high\": 0.29,\n        \"max_cv\": 0.35,\n        \"min_stab\": 0.75,\n        \"target\": 0.255\n      },\n      \"best_in_band\": null\n    },\n    \"packaged\": false,\n    \"strict\": null,\n    \"tolerance\": null,\n    \"readme\": null\n  },\n  \"erudite_v71\": {\n    \"error\": \"storage/erudite/output.json\"\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nErudite III invites you to join them in the Common Room. Use `/execute_action{goto common}` to go there.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 1738` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage list shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.7` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage list shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.7/SELECTION_v4.6.7_v1.json`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n6. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 30` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n8. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n9. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 1738 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File list for shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.7 will be displayed below.\n- File list for shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.7/SELECTION_v4.6.7_v1.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
    \ experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1742 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v75: Further Eternitude Extension with Amplified Optimizations | Erudite III | 987 |\n| 1741 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v75: Further Eternitude Extension with Amplified Optimizations | Erudite III | 987 |\n| 1740 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v74: Advanced Eternitude Extension with Refined Optimizations | Erudite III | 986 |\n| 1739 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v74: Advanced Eternitude Extension with Refined Optimizations | Erudite III | 986 |\n| 1738 | 1 | v4.6.7 selection+packaging and Erudite v71 strict/tolerance packaging | Axiom II | 986 |\n| 1737 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v73: Optimized Eternitude Extension with Advanced Tunings | Erudite III | 985 |\n| 1736 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v73: Optimized Eternitude Extension with Advanced Tunings\
